window.SEARCH_INDEX=[{"u": "sign-in.html", "t": "Sign in", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Sign in", "x": "Use the Login screen to sign in to TireWorks HD and choose the store you work in."}, {"u": "sign-in.html#sign-in-with-a-tireworks-hd-account", "t": "Sign in with a TireWorks HD account", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Sign in", "x": "Enter your User Name . The user name is not case sensitive. Enter your Password . The password is case sensitive. Select the store you want from the list of available locations. Use the search box to find a store by location number or location name. If you have access to only one store, TireWorks HD logs you directly into that store. If your store uses iPOSPays, select a credit card terminal when you are asked, after you pick the store. See Electronic Payments ."}, {"u": "sign-in.html#sign-in-with-your-windows-account", "t": "Sign in with your Windows account", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Sign in", "x": "Before you start: A manager must first map your Windows account to your TireWorks HD user at Manage; Company Setup; Users , on the Windows Authentication tab. Select Windows Authentication instead of TireWorks HD Authentication . User Name fills in with your Windows login. Password is not used. Select Login ."}, {"u": "home-page.html", "t": "Home page", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Home page", "x": "The Home page is where you start most of your work. It holds the application toolbar and tabs that list your store's quotes, appointments, orders, transfers and purchases."}, {"u": "home-page.html#change-your-store", "t": "Change your store", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Home page", "x": "Select the location and user button . A list of the stores your access rights allow appears. Select the store you want."}, {"u": "home-page.html#application-toolbar", "t": "Application toolbar", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Home page", "x": "The toolbar menus open the main areas of TireWorks HD. TireWorks : Current Session Info, My Preferences, Lock My Session, Change Password, Logout and Exit. Current Session Info : shows your login, the store you are logged into, your security profile for that store, your Windows login, the computer name and IP address, the TireWorks HD version, and memory and CPU use. My Preferences : opens your own user record, where you can change your Details , User Settings and Print Settings . If your store uses iPOSPays, it also has a Credit Card Terminal tab. See Electronic Payments . If the fields in My Preferences are grayed out, your access rights do not allow you to change them. Exit : exiting, or closing TireWorks HD with the X, asks \"Are you sure you want to exit?\" Select Yes to close. New : create a new Customer, Customer Deposit, Customer ROA, QuickQuote, Appointment, Service Request, Transfer, Purchase Order, Inventory Receipt, Inventory Adjustment, AP Invoice or Payroll Entry. You add a vehicle from the customer or the order, not from the New menu. Items your access rights do not allow are grayed out. Service Request does not show at all if you are not allowed to create a service request from the New menu. AP Invoice : See AP Invoices and Vendor Credits . Find : search for a Customer, Customer Deposit, Quick Quote, Appointment, Service Request (open and historical sales documents), Transfer, Purchase Order, Inventory Receipt, Inventory Adjustment, AP Invoice or ROA. Cash Drawer : shows total daily sales by payment method and the total transaction count. You can reconcile the drawer, produce the cash drawer reconciliation report, and manage petty cash. Manage : configure and manage setup information, location management, access rights, pricing, special programs and more. Report : Audited Events, Customer Deposit, and My Reports (the inventory, purchasing, sales and other reports your access rights allow). Skins : change the screen colors. Help : About (software version), User Manual, Video Library (training videos), and Refresh User Session. Use Refresh User Session instead of logging out and back in when someone with the access rights to do so makes changes. Tip: Many windows also have a (?) help icon. Hover over it for a tip, and click it to open the training video for that window, where one is set up."}, {"u": "home-page.html#home-page-tabs", "t": "Home page tabs", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Home page", "x": "Quick Quote : lists all saved quick quotes, with the date created, customer, vehicle, contact information, quoted by and any comments. Filter to the user logged in . Filter by salesman, customer or quick quote number . Hover over a quote to text the customer or open Customer Communication. See Customer Communication (Texting) . Appointments : an electronic appointment calendar for managing multiple service types, bays and more. The calendar shows one day by default. Week, month and timeline displays are also available. You can print calendars for a single day or a date range. Print all appointments or confirmed appointments only. The legend at the top shows what each appointment color means: Pending customer approval, Confirmed appointments, Customer is waiting, Vehicle not arrived, Vehicle dropped off, Waiting for parts, Order In Process, Order Completed, and Vehicle has been Delivered. An appointment that is split among multiple calendars shows (*Multi) . Use New Appointment , Search and Print below the calendar. Configure Calendars : choose which of your store's calendars you see, and in what order. Move calendars between Available and Configured with the arrow buttons. Use the up and down arrows to change the display order, and then select OK . Your choice is saved for you at this store only. If Configure Calendars is missing or grayed out, your access rights do not allow it ( Appointments - Configure Calendars ). Managers set up the store's calendars at Manage; Location Setup; Calendars . Note: If your store uses the Auto Cancel Appointments Duration setting, appointments still open that many days after the appointment date are canceled automatically when someone logs in to the store. Service Request : lists all open service requests, with the service request number, promised time, status, approval, service rep, customer name, vehicle, plate number, created date, contact information, order total, program, unit number, last modified date and comments. Show My Orders : shows only orders where you are the salesperson. You can set it to start checked in your User Settings . Filter by salesman, customer, order number, PO number, reference number, order comments, transfer number, unit number, vehicle (year, make, model, plate or comments), contact, or DR number . Filter by special program . Order Total shows a full circle when the order is fully paid and a half circle when it is partially paid. Hover over the circle to see the payment status. Approval shows whether a customer approval request is still pending. See Customer Approval . DOT Check : if your store uses TireMetrix TRP, type a DOT number and select Check to check it right away. Add, remove or reorder columns at Manage; Location Setup; Search Results Configuration ( Home Screen - Service Request List ). Inspections : lists inspections from TCS Inspect. See TCS Inspect . Transfers : lists all unreceived transfers, with the transfer ID, sending location, receiving location, order number, customer name, status, created date, created by and comments. Filter by salesman, customer or transfer number . Store Performance : shows a configurable report of store performance. Purchases : lists all unreceived purchase orders, with the PO number, vendor name, status, delivery date, user ID, date created, date completed, reference number and comments. Filter by vendor, user or purchase order number . Cycle Count : provides a daily count list based on your cycle count configuration. See cycle counts previously performed and processed ."}, {"u": "home-page.html#common-icons", "t": "Common icons", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Home page", "x": "These icons appear on the Home page, on its tabs and throughout the application. Refreshes the Home page. Starts a quick quote from anywhere this icon appears. Starts a service request from anywhere this icon appears. Searches all document types, customers, ROAs or customer deposits. Quick tire search. Search by size, Mfg sku or Mfg. Abbreviation. Add Vehicle : shows below Quick Tire Search on the Service Request tab. Enter a vehicle to start a Quick Quote with that vehicle and open F1 Tire Lookup on its first tire fitment. If the plate or VIN matches an existing customer, you are asked whether to use that customer and vehicle. If the catalog has no tire fitments for the vehicle, \"No tire fitments were found for the vehicle!\" displays. Changes the font size of the tire search screen. Locks your session and displays a login window for the next user to log in. Displays at the bottom of the login screen so you can log back in when you come back to the computer."}, {"u": "configure-tire-lookup-search-results.html", "t": "Configure tire lookup search results", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Configure tire lookup search results", "x": "Use Search Results Configuration to choose what shows on your search results screen. Each user can set up their own search results."}, {"u": "configure-tire-lookup-search-results.html#open-search-results-configuration", "t": "Open Search Results Configuration", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Configure tire lookup search results", "x": "In the F1 Tire Lookup search screen, right-click any line item and select Configure Search Results . The Search Results Configuration window opens for the list you right-clicked. Tip: Right-click works the same way on other lists that support it, such as the Home screen tabs. Note: A user with the Search Results Configuration - User Selection access right can pick another user at the top right and set up that user's results. Note: Managers can also open this window at Manage; Location Setup; Search Results Configuration ."}, {"u": "configure-tire-lookup-search-results.html#add-search-fields", "t": "Add search fields", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Configure tire lookup search results", "x": "Verify that Search Type is set to Tire Lookup . In the Available Fields list, highlight the field you want to show in the search results, and then select . The field moves to Assigned Fields . Repeat until every field you want has been moved to Assigned Fields . Use the arrows to arrange the fields in the order they display, from left to right."}, {"u": "configure-tire-lookup-search-results.html#add-sort-columns", "t": "Add sort columns", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Configure tire lookup search results", "x": "Follow the same steps to add Sort Columns . At least one sort column is needed to save. Select . Select Save . Note: If the changes do not show right away, select Help; Refresh User Session ."}, {"u": "subscribe-to-reports.html", "t": "Subscribe to reports", "p": "Section 1: Login Screen & Home Page › Subscribe to reports", "x": "Use a report subscription to schedule a report for delivery by email, to a shared file, or both. You set up each subscription by report. Open your web browser and go to your report server's web portal. Get the web portal address from your administrator or TCS Support. If prompted, sign in with the report account your administrator gave you. Select the folder where the report is housed. Locate the report you want. Select the menu ( ... or down arrow) to the right of the report name, and then select Subscribe . Fill in the Report Delivery Options for email or shared file delivery. For shared file delivery, enter the file share path and the user name and password your administrator gives you. Enter the schedule for the subscription to run. Fill in the report parameter values. The parameters depend on the report you selected."}, {"u": "quotes.html", "t": "Quotes", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "Use Quick Quote to price tires and services for a customer without opening a service request. You can save the quote, move it onto the appointment calendar, or convert it to a service request."}, {"u": "quotes.html#start-a-quote", "t": "Start a quote", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "On the Home Page, select Quick Quote . You can also start a quote from the Quick Quote tab or from New; QuickQuote . Enter any one or combination of Last Name , First Name or Phone Number , and then select Lookup . Select the customer from the list, and then select Done . If no results display, enter the first name, last name and phone number. These are required to save the quote. Select or add a vehicle. For an existing customer with vehicles, choose the vehicle and select Select Vehicle . If the customer has several vehicles, use the Filter option to narrow the vehicle list. Select the Tire Fitment from the drop-down list. For a new customer, select Start New Vehicle and complete the information you know. You must enter Year , Make , Model and Engine . At stores that use the TireGuide catalog, enter Year , Make , Model and Option . To skip vehicle selection and go straight to adding services, use these search buttons : F1 : tire and wheel search only. F2 : parts and labor search. F3 : complete inventory search. The description field is searchable."}, {"u": "quotes.html#search-for-tires-f1", "t": "Search for tires (F1)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "If a vehicle and fitment were selected, or you created a vehicle and filled in its fitment, search results display automatically. If no vehicle was added, the search screen opens without results. In Global Lookup , enter a simple tire size (for example, 2255018) and press Enter. You can filter the results by speed rating. You can filter the results by any part of the description. You can also narrow the search with any of the options shown below. Double-click the highlighted tire you want to select it, or select up to three tires to compare."}, {"u": "quotes.html#compare-tires-with-tire-quote", "t": "Compare tires with Tire Quote", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "Before you start: Tire Quote needs the Service Request - Tire Quote access right. If the Tire Quote (F2) button is missing on the tire lookup screen, your access rights do not allow it. After selecting up to three tires, select Tire Quote . The quote shows the selected tires with their features and their prices for quantities of 1, 2 or 4. You can print the Tire Quote. You can select the tires the customer chose and add them to the quote. Change the Package , Price Level , Tax Rate or Other Qty if needed. Other Qty is a quantity other than 1, 2 or 4. Use Include Add-Ons? , Include Road Hazard? , Include Nitrogen? and Include Tire Disposal? to choose which package items are included in the quoted price. Include Nitrogen? and Include Tire Disposal? show only if your store charges those fees. See Tire Package Fees ."}, {"u": "quotes.html#add-tires-without-the-tire-package", "t": "Add tires without the tire package", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "Select Add Selected Items to add the tires directly to the quote without the default tire package line items. Tip: Use Add Selected Items for carry-out quotes or wholesale situations. Change the price if needed, either by typing it in or by adjusting the profit meter. What you can change depends on your access rights. Enter the information, and then select Done ."}, {"u": "quotes.html#add-a-package-f2", "t": "Add a package (F2)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "Use the F2 screen to add a package from the list. In the Lookup field, enter a short part of the package description. Double-click the package you want. Follow the wizard through the catalog selections. When the wizard finishes, a message confirms that the package was added. Continue adding packages, or select X in the upper-right corner to close the screen."}, {"u": "quotes.html#add-parts-by-hand-f2", "t": "Add parts by hand (F2)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "Before you start: The Parts and Labor tabs are not shown at stores that use the TireGuide catalog. If the vehicle was typed in by hand and is not in the catalog, \"Vehicle not found in catalog. Parts and Labor tabs would be disabled.\" displays and the tabs cannot be used. Select the Parts tab. Select the supplier. The default suppliers display first. Select the category. Select the group. Instead, you can enter a keyword in Lookup and select Search . When Lookup has text, the search uses only that text and ignores Category and Group . Check the box to the left of the part you want. Pick a part whose availability shows YES . Select the package to add the part to. Select Add Parts to Order . Continue adding parts, or select X in the upper-right corner to close the screen."}, {"u": "quotes.html#add-labor-by-hand-f2", "t": "Add labor by hand (F2)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "Select the Labor tab. Follow the same steps as for parts. Note: The hourly rate comes from the store setting in TireWorks HD."}, {"u": "quotes.html#search-all-inventory-f3", "t": "Search all inventory (F3)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "Use F3 to search your complete inventory by description. Double-click the item to add it. Fill in the dialog box as needed, and select the package to add the item to. The fields you can change depend on your access rights. Select Done . Continue adding items, or select X in the upper-right corner to close the screen."}, {"u": "quotes.html#add-a-discount-to-a-quote", "t": "Add a discount to a quote", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "You can add a discount by hand, or set up discounts and coupons to apply automatically. Select Total Discount at the bottom left of the quote screen, under the order totals. Highlight the branch or the specific line item in the tree that the discount applies to. Select Add... . Enter the Discount Type : a flat discount or a percentage discount. Select a reason code from the list. Enter comments if you want. Select Done . Note: Discounts and coupons of different classes do not stack. The one that gives the customer the greatest benefit is used. Coupons of the same class can be combined. See Discount Maintenance ."}, {"u": "quotes.html#save-or-convert-the-quote", "t": "Save or convert the quote", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Quotes", "x": "When the quote is ready, choose one of these options. Save : saves the quote, which then displays on the Quick Quote tab of the Home Page. If your store uses the Auto Cancel Quotes Duration setting, open quotes are canceled automatically after that many days, when someone logs in to the store. Create Appt. : moves the quote onto the appointment calendar. Create Service Request : converts the quote to a service request. If your store uses the Update Cost Upon QuickQuote Conversion setting, item costs may be refreshed from each item's default cost when the quote is converted. Note: Whether saving a Quick Quote or Appointment commits inventory depends on the store's Quotes Commit Inventory checkbox ( Manage; Location Setup; Locations , Misc Settings tab). When it is not checked, inventory is not committed until the quote is converted to a service request. Note: Order Validation rules also apply to Quick Quotes and Appointments. See Order Validation ."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html", "t": "Creating a service request", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Use a service request to write up the tires and services for a customer and vehicle, then complete the work, take payment and invoice the order."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#start-the-order-and-find-the-customer", "t": "Start the order and find the customer", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "On the Home Page, select on the Service Request tab, or select NEW Service Request . In Customer Lookup , enter any one or combination of the lookup fields to search TireWorks HD customer records. TireWorks HD searches the customer file for a match based on the fields you fill in. If no results are returned, select to add a new customer. See Add a new customer below. Enter the new customer's information. The customer information screen opens so you can verify the customer and select or create a vehicle. Select Done . The customer displays on the service request automatically. If the customer is found, highlight the customer and select Done . The customer information screen opens so you can verify the customer and select or create a vehicle. Select Done . The customer displays on the service request automatically."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-a-new-customer", "t": "Add a new customer", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Select the Customer Type : Household or Business . Household lets you add several members, along with their vehicles, to one account. History is kept in the main household account. Enter the name and address information. Enter the contact information. Select the Contact Type and Phone Type . Select Add . The number is added to the phone number list as the default. To change the default, select the green check mark to the left of the contact type. To delete a number, select the red minus symbol to the left of the contact type. Select Done . The Customer ID is generated automatically from set criteria, for example the first few characters of the last name, the store number and the number of times that ID has been used. The customer displays on the service request automatically."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-a-number-for-text-messages", "t": "Add a number for text messages", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Add a text contact so you can send the customer texts . When your company uses two-way texting, customers can reply, and their replies show in the SMS Hub (see Customer Communication ). If your company is not set up for two-way texting, texts are one-way and customers cannot reply. Select the Contact Type Text . A Phone contact with Phone Type Cell can also receive texts. Select the Cell Provider . This field displays, and is needed, only when your company is not set up for two-way texting. Enter the cell number. Select Add . The number is added to the phone number list. The number displays on the service request as a send text icon."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#view-and-edit-customer-information", "t": "View and edit customer information", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "After you find or create the customer, select the customer (in white) on the left side of the service request to view the customer information. Selected Customer : lets you edit member details: First Name, Last Name, Gender and Contact Information. Address : lets you edit address information. Bill To Customer : lets you change the Bill To Customer without changing the customer the services are performed for. Select to view or edit the customer's details. What you can see and change depends on your access rights. The customer record has these tabs: General : the salesperson assigned, credit limit, payment terms and similar settings. Members : household members, their contact information and comments. Addresses : address information. A customer may have more than one address. Vehicle : vehicle information. Customer Rules : additional customer pricing, if required, on top of the store's default price level. Order History : the customer's order history and summary information. To view archived history, select . Financial Summary : for an accounts receivable customer, shows current and past-due amounts, and lets you view open receivables and all transactions. The customer information panel also includes: Household Members : select the right household member, or add a new member. Carry-out Order : marks the order as carry-out, so package information is not added automatically. Vehicles : select an existing vehicle for the order, start a new vehicle, or deactivate a vehicle. Deactivating a vehicle does not remove its history. Use the filter for longer vehicle lists. Note: To assign a special program at the member or vehicle level, select the ellipses to the right of the member name or vehicle."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-a-new-vehicle", "t": "Add a new vehicle", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Enter the vehicle information using one of these three options. Plate : enter the plate number, select the state and select . The state defaults to the servicing store's state. If a match is found, all vehicle information fills in automatically. Enter the color and next inspection if you know them. You can fill these in later. VIN : enter the VIN and select to fill in the vehicle information automatically. Enter the plate, color and next inspection. You can fill these in later. By hand : enter the year, make, model and engine yourself, when the VIN or plate is not known. Enter the plate, color and next inspection. You can fill these in later. Note: Year , Make , Model and Engine are required. At stores that use the TireGuide catalog, the fourth field is Option (trim or submodel) instead of Engine . Keep these vehicle field rules in mind: Mileage : shows the vehicle's last recorded mileage and cannot be typed over. To change it, select Set to open Update Mileage , and then enter the Correct Mileage . VIN : takes letters and numbers only. A VIN lookup needs at least 11 characters. CARFAX QuickVin : if it returns more than one vehicle, pick the right one from the list. Note: A vehicle typed in by hand, rather than picked from the catalog lists, can still be used, but the F2 Parts and Labor tabs cannot be used for it."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#view-and-edit-vehicle-information", "t": "View and edit vehicle information", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Select the vehicle (in white) on the left side of the service request to view its information. Selected Vehicle : shows the vehicle the vehicle data is for. Select to edit the vehicle information. Details : lists the vehicle's details. You can edit them on the Summary tab. Summary tab: shows the vehicle's details and lets you edit them. If the vehicle has multiple (staggered) fitments, check the box, and front and rear selection boxes display. Select the front and rear fitment from the drop-down lists, based on the VIN entered. Enter the unit ID, if there is one. Select the duty type. Normal is selected by default. If the VIN is wrong, select Change and enter the correct VIN. Tire Fitments tab: shows the fitments available for the vehicle information provided, in more detail. It gives the standard tire size, inflation, rim width, bolt pattern and TPMS information. At stores that use the TireGuide catalog, this tab is Tire Fitment Details . Oil Settings tab: lists the recommended oil type, viscosity and capacity. You can also set the customer's requested oil type and viscosity. Conditions tab: lists vehicle conditions you may need to gather for proper service, for example automatic transmission, turbo or air conditioning. Vin Details tab: lists any details for the VIN. Vehicle Specs. tab: lists all vehicle specifications. History tab: lists the vehicle's history, which you can print. Select to see all vehicle history that has been submitted to Carfax. You can also view archived service history from your previous POS system. If you chose the wrong vehicle, select to return to the vehicle list. Note: The Oil Settings , Conditions and Vin Details tabs are not shown at stores that use the TireGuide catalog."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-tires-and-services", "t": "Add tires and services", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Select the search that fits what you are adding: Tire Search : search for tires. Package Search : search for service packages, parts and labor. Total Inventory Search : search your complete inventory. Add Vehicle : on the F1, F2 and F3 screens, adds a vehicle to the order without closing the screen. The vehicle is assigned to the order right away, so its tire fitment can be used in the search. It is not shown on carry-out orders or on the F4 Diagnosticator."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#tire-lookup-screen", "t": "Tire lookup screen", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "The tire lookup screen has these fields and columns. Global Lookup : a 3-segment universal SKU. Segment 1 is the simple tire size, with no dashes, slashes or letters. Segment 2 is the manufacturer code, generally the first 3 characters of the manufacturer. Segment 3 is the manufacturer item number. Show Inactive Tires : search results display all tires, active or inactive. Tire Fitment : defaults to the tire fitment selected for the vehicle. You can choose other fitments. Speed Rating : defaults based on the tire fitment. Price Level : defaults to the store's default, or to the account default for an A/R customer. Filter : narrows the search by any part of the description. Advanced Filter : applies additional filters based on the inventory tree structure. Quantity Available : total quantity on hand less committed quantity. Warehouse Quantity : warehouse and distributor quantities and price. If there are several warehouses, you can set it to display only the default servicing warehouse. ASL Quantity : quantity and price held at all other stores. Price : the customer's price, set by the store's default price level or the A/R account price level, plus any additional price rules. Tire Detail : specs, picture, features, comps and warranty information. This is available only for tires housed in TDC (Tire Data Central), a database of over 105,000 tires. Additional Search Filtering : more filters to narrow the search results further. Filtering by Item Group : see Item Group Setup and Item Assignment ."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-tires-with-tire-search", "t": "Add tires with Tire Search", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "If a vehicle and tire fitment are defined in the vehicle information, Tire Search displays only the tires that meet the fitment requirements. Only tires with the minimum speed rating or higher display. If the fitment is not defined or not available, you can use Global Lookup . Select (highlight) the tires you want. Select Tire Quote (F2) or Add Selected Item (F1) . Tire Quote adds the tire package automatically unless you specify otherwise in the quote. Select the correct number of tires. The tires and package fill in on the service request. Add Selected Item adds only the selected tires. It is generally used for carry-out or commercial tires. If you used Add Selected Item , check the pop-up window, and make changes or add information as needed. Price and cost default from the price level and average cost. FET fills in if it applies. The product code fills in based on special program requirements. If you cannot change the Prod. Code on a special program order, your access rights do not allow it (Special Program: Service Request - Prod. Code). You can set the technician and actual hours. The package fills in based on the store's tire package default. The profit meter shows the Profit %. Move the profit bar to change the price to the profit % you want. You can also click anywhere on the GP% meter to jump to that profit %. Your access rights can limit price changes: Raising a price beyond what your user's hand pricing allows needs Service Request - Price Increase. Going below the minimum profit percent set for your user needs Service Request - Bypass Price Validation. If you cannot change prices by hand, Calculate can still save a new price, but only if you have Item Detail Popup - Calculate Increase or Calculate Decrease. The item description can be changed only for SKU types set up to allow it (for California BAR compliance), or by users with Service Request - Item Description. Select Done . The item fills in on the service request."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#view-item-details-and-time-logs", "t": "View item details and time logs", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "To see an item's full information later, hover to the left of the line and select Item Detail (the blue \"i\"). The Item Detail window has these tabs: Item Detail , Core , Pricing , Site Detail , On Order , User Defined , Item History , Supplier Info , Item Allocation , Item Movement and Unit of Measurement . Note: Each tab needs its own access right, so you may not see all of them. In the line item window, View Time Log next to Actual Hours shows each technician's start and end times, total time and stop reason."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#approve-decline-or-delete-a-tire-package", "t": "Approve, decline or delete a tire package", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Hover over on the tire package tab , and select approve package . The informational \"i\" is replaced with a green check mark, showing that the customer approved the package (Ready For Work status). To decline the package later, use the same method and select decline package . To delete the package completely, select the minus sign on the right side of the package tab, and then answer Yes in the confirmation window. The tire package tab also has these options: : select it if you want it, or set it up to be added automatically. : available if a TPMS package has been created. : if the tires are not available, select it to source the items. See Sourcing Manager ."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-a-service-package-with-package-search", "t": "Add a service package with Package Search", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Select Package Search , and then select the Service Package tab. Enter the package type, for example oil or brakes. marks a customer preference. marks a package recommended by Epicor. marks the last service performed. Double-click the package you want. If your store uses Epicor ISE and the catalog asks vehicle condition questions, answer each one. There is no Cancel . A question left unanswered is set to \"don't know\" where that answer is allowed. Select the supplier. If your store uses Epicor ISE, a supplier's alternate store is listed as its own line, named \"[Seller] - [Alt. Location]\". The Your Qty. column shows what is in your store's inventory. Price column colors follow the legend on the screen: white is Customer Pricing (your store's price for items you stock), yellow is Real-time Supplier Pricing, and red is No Price Available. Supplier pricing displays in the Vendor Cost column. To hide items with zero available quantity, select . Check the item you prefer, and then select . Note: Double-clicking a part or labor item does not add it. Check the item, and then select Done . The next item to select displays. Repeat the steps above for it. Select Done . The message \"package successfully added to service request\" displays, and the service request shows a new tab for the service package. If items are not available in your inventory, select to source them. See Sourcing Manager ."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-parts-with-parts-search", "t": "Add parts with Parts Search", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Before you start: The Parts and Labor tabs are not shown at stores that use the TireGuide catalog, and cannot be used for a vehicle typed in by hand. See the note under Add parts by hand (F2) in Quotes. Select Parts Search , and then select the Parts tab. Select the Supplier from the drop-down list. Select the Category and Group . Check the box of the part you want. Add the part to the service request in one of two ways: To add it on its own, select , verify or enter the cost, and then select Done . The part is added under the miscellaneous service tab. To add it to an existing package, select , select the package from the drop-down list, verify or enter the cost, and then select Done . The part is added to that package. This is generally used when a Miscellaneous Service Package already exists."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-labor-with-labor-search", "t": "Add labor with Labor Search", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Select Labor Search , and then select the Labor tab. Follow the same steps as for parts."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#create-a-non-catalog-part", "t": "Create a non-catalog part", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Use Create Part to create a non-catalog part record, assign it to the right nodes of the inventory tree and set up its part information. Select the Create Part icon. Select the right value from the drop-down list for each node. Enter the part information. Select the Create Part icon."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#header-information", "t": "Header information", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "The header of the service request holds these fields. Consignment sale : check this if the sale is a consignment sale. Tire Tax Exempt : check this if tires on this order are tax exempt. For an A/R customer, it defaults from the customer record settings. Vehicle Data : enter insurance and tread depth information. It can be made a required field (see Order Validation ). Vehicle Data holds Insurer Name , Policy # and Dually Vehicle? , plus the Tire Tread Depth (Outer, Mid and Inner for each tire), Tire Inflation and Brakes tabs. It is available only when a vehicle is on the order, so it cannot be used on carry-out orders. Created : defaults to the user logged in. You can change it from the drop-down list. Hand Ticket : enter the number if you use Road Service Hand Tickets as a reference. Customer PO : enter a purchase order number if you want. It is required when the A/R customer's record flags the PO as required. Salesperson : defaults to the user logged in, unless the A/R customer has a default set in the customer record. You can change it from the drop-down list. Tax Detail : defaults to the store's tax rate, unless the A/R customer has a tax rate set in the customer record. You can change it from the drop-down list. Mileage in: and out: : enter Mileage In. Mileage Out defaults to the same value. When Mileage In is filled in, becomes available. See below. Mileage In and Out can be entered only when a vehicle is on the order. Removing the vehicle clears them. You are prompted if the Mileage Out you enter is not valid. Price Level : defaults to the store's price level, unless the A/R customer has a price level set in the customer record. Special Program : select a special program, such as Goodyear National Accounts. You are asked questions about the program and shown its requirements. If the program has its own price level, the order's price level changes to it. The order is processed through to the manufacturer of the national account program. Select Order Requirements to see and answer the program's requirements on the order. Promise Time : the completion time promised to the customer. It can be set to display on the service request. The time filled in on a new order depends on your store's settings, for example Customer Waiting, the current time, a set number of minutes later, or a set time of day. It may also add the service duration of the work on the order. Unchecking Customer Waiting clears the Promise Time."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#look-up-symptoms-with-the-diagnosticator", "t": "Look up symptoms with the Diagnosticator", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Before you start: F4 Diagnosticator and F6 Factory Scheduled Maintenance are not shown at stores that use the TireGuide catalog. F4 is also hidden on Goodyear National Account orders. Select the Diagnosticator icon, or press F4 . Enter the symptom. Recommended diagnostics display."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#get-factory-scheduled-maintenance", "t": "Get factory scheduled maintenance", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Factory Scheduled Maintenance suggests maintenance based on the vehicle's current mileage. Select FSM , or press F6 . Fill in the vehicle conditions if required. You can also fill them in on the vehicle record. Select Done . Recommendations display, highlighted based on the Mileage In entry. You can switch Driving Conditions between Severe and Normal . You can also set this on the vehicle record. By default, all recommendations are selected to be added. You can print or cancel the recommendations without affecting the order. Select, add or decline services based on the customer's preference. Added services show on the service request as individual tabs, one per service. All declined services display in one tab and print on page 2 of the invoice. Declined services are also visible on the customer's future orders. You can also see the declined services for other vehicles in the household, and create an appointment for them."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#review-services-with-service-advisor", "t": "Review services with Service Advisor", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "When a vehicle is on the order, the Service Advisor panel on the service request shows counts of Recommended Services, TCS Inspect Recommendations, Previously Declined Services and any Carfax Recalls. Select Service Advisor to open the TireWorks HD Advisor window. The Current Vehicle tab lists Recommended Services, TCS Inspect Recommendations, Previously Declined Services and Reported Recall(s) for the vehicle. Each service shows its Last Date , Last Mileage and Package Price . For a declined service, the price is what it was when the customer declined it. For each service, choose one of these: Add to Order Add As Declined Don't Ask Again : the service stops being suggested for this vehicle. Schedule Future Appointment To see recommended and declined services for the customer's other vehicles, select the Household Vehicles tab. Select Load more vehicles... to see more. Select Done to apply your choices, or select Cancel . Note: A declined service drops off Previously Declined Services once it is invoiced at the same store, added to an order, or marked Don't Ask Again."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#assign-technicians", "t": "Assign technicians", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "You can assign technicians to the service request as a whole or to single line items. You can select up to two technicians per line item ( Tech. 1 and Tech. 2 ), or four if your company has that option turned on. Note: You can change technicians freely on an open order. Changing them on a closed order needs the Service Request - Technician Assignments access right. Select Technician (in white) on the left side of the service request . Highlight the line to assign technicians to. Select the technicians from the drop-down lists. Select Done ."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-order-comments", "t": "Add order comments", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Order comments apply to the whole order. Public comments print. Private comments stay with the order and do not print. Before you start: Seeing and editing the comment boxes needs the Service Request - Order Public Comments or Order Private Comments access right. If you cannot see or edit a comment box, your access rights do not allow it. Users with EDIT on those rights can also add or change order comments on closed and invoiced orders. Select Order Comments (in white) on the left side of the service request . Enter the comments in the right section. Select Done . Tip: Use Find Comments to pick commonly used comments, so you do not have to type them. See Comment Setup & Maintenance ."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#change-shop-fees", "t": "Change shop fees", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Shop fees can be order based, package based, or not used at all. They are set as a percentage, with an optional minimum fee, maximum fee or both. Fees can be charged on parts, labor or both, and can be taxable, discountable or both. Note: Managers set up shop fees for each store at Manage; Company Setup; Other Fees & Charges , Shop Fees tab. Copy Shop Fee Settings copies a finished setup to other stores. You can change the shop fee from its default on any order. Select Shop Fees (in white) on the left side of the service request . Enter the charge you want, or 0.00, and select Freeze . Note: Changing or freezing the shop fee needs EDIT on the Service Request - Shop Fee access right."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#review-order-totals", "t": "Review order totals", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Order Totals shows the order subtotal and tax, and the GP for Tires, Other and the Order. The GP meters update right away when a discount is added to the order. Select Order Totals (in white) on the left side of the service request."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#add-a-discount-to-a-service-request", "t": "Add a discount to a service request", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "You can apply a discount to the service request as a whole or to any single line item. Select $0.00 (in white) on the left side of the service request. Highlight the level for the discount: The service request as a whole. Any line items individually. Select Add... . Select the Discount Type from the drop-down list: Flat Discount or Percentage Discount . Enter the amount. Select the Reason Code . See Discount Maintenance . Add comments if you want. They are not required. Select Done . Select Done in the discount details window too. The discount displays in the discount column on the lines it applies to, based on the level you chose. It also displays in the discount box on the left and at Pkg. Discount in the body of the service request. Note: Discounts and coupons of different classes do not stack. The one that gives the customer the greatest benefit is used. Coupons of the same class can be combined. When you select Add Payment , discounts and coupons that have expired or been made inactive are checked: Users with the Service Request - Expired Discount access right are asked \"Would you still like to allow this discount or coupon to be used?\" Everyone else is told the discount or coupon will be removed and the order total will change. Discounts and coupons marked Honor After Expiration are not removed."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#complete-the-order", "t": "Complete the order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Select Complete Order to mark the work as done and set the order to Work Complete. You do not have to complete the order before Add Payment . To reopen a Work Complete order, select Revise Order . The order returns to Ready For Work."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#check-the-validation-icon", "t": "Check the validation icon", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "The validation icon in the top-right corner shows whether the order meets its validation and sourcing requirements. This is separate from the order status. See Order statuses below. : the order is in good status and is ready for payment collection and invoicing. : the order is incomplete and cannot be completed until its requirements are met. Select the icon to see the unfulfilled requirements, then fill in the required information or complete the required tasks. ? : the order is missing validation requirements only."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#take-payment-and-invoice-the-order", "t": "Take payment and invoice the order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "When the order is finished, use Add Payment to collect payment, convert the order to an invoice, and print or email the invoice. The order is then Closed. Select Add Payment (in white) on the left side of the service request . If a customer deposit was taken, it may be listed on the payment screen . See Customer Deposit . Select the payment type from the drop-down list. Store Account does not display for household customers, business customers with a $0 credit limit, or customers who are past due or set to No House Credit. Customers set to Cash Only can pay by cash only. Enter the payment amount. Select Apply . If the customer is paying with more than one payment type, repeat until the remaining due is $0. Select Done . \"Remaining Due is $0.00, Would you like to Complete this Order now?\" displays. Select Yes . The invoice displays so you can print or email it. The default printer, number of copies and print options can also be set at the user level. Note: When the System Setting Suppress Confirm Complete Order Dialog is on, Add Payment works differently. Add Payment opens only after all Block order validations are met and all items are sourced and received. The Done button reads Invoice Order , and selecting it invoices the order right away with no confirmation. Card payments are processed when you select Invoice Order . Payments cannot be saved without invoicing: closing the payment screen asks you to confirm, then removes all payments except Customer Deposits and Text-to-Pay link payments."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#order-statuses", "t": "Order statuses", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Every order has a status that shows where it is in the workflow. The status displays on the order and in order search results. Service Request statuses are set for you. Each package on the order has its own status, and the order shows the least advanced status of any package on it. For example, one package waiting on a part keeps the whole order at Waiting For Parts. Quick Quote, Appointment, Work Complete, Closed, Memo, Declined and Canceled come from an action you take instead. Status names can be changed for each store on the OrderState Labels tab (see Locations Setup and Maintenance ). The names below are the defaults. Status numbers are listed in the Appendix. Quick Quote : the order was started from Quick Quote. It stays a Quick Quote until it is converted. Appointment : the order was created from the Appointment Calendar. It stays an Appointment until it is converted to a service request. Open : a tire or catalog part still needs to be resolved before its package can be approved. Also shown when every package left on the order has been declined. Estimate : services are added but not yet approved by the customer. Approved : the customer approved the work, but at least one item still needs to be sourced. Waiting For Parts : at least one item is on a purchase order or transfer that has not been fully received. Ready For Work : every approved item is in hand: in stock, received, or not needing sourcing. Revise Order also returns a Work Complete order to this status. Work Complete : Complete Order was selected. The work is done and the order is ready for Add Payment. The order is still editable, and Revise Order reopens it. Revised : a Work Complete order that was changed afterward. This is mostly seen on older orders. Revise Order now returns an order to Ready For Work instead. Closed : payment was added and the invoice created. The order cannot be edited, but it can be copied or reversed (see Invoice Reversal and Copy ). Memo : the order was saved as a memo instead of an invoice. This happens at Add Payment when every line left on the order is a fee with no price and no cost. Declined : every package on the order was declined. This is set when you save and answer Yes to \"The Order contains only declined services. Do you want to decline the order?\" Canceled : the order was canceled with Cancel Order ."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#toolbar-and-line-item-tools", "t": "Toolbar and line item tools", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "The service request toolbar and line items have these other tools. Save : saves the order. Save periodically as you work. Save and Close : saves the order, closes it and returns to the Home Page. Back : returns to the Home Page. : adds a whole string of information for a commonly used SKU (for example, PUMP, 2, 25.00) and fills in the complete line. Add Comment : hover to the left of a line item and select the comment icon. The comment window has a Public box, which prints, and a Private box, which is kept with the order and does not print. If you cannot see or edit one of the boxes, your access rights do not allow it (Service Request - Line Item Public Comments or Line Item Private Comments)."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#delete-a-line", "t": "Delete a line", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Hover to the left of the line item and select the red circled minus sign. Confirm that you want to delete the line. If the line is on an open or partially received purchase order, the Associated PO window displays the PO number, status, vendor and SKUs. Choose how to handle the PO: Complete PO : creates and processes an inventory receipt for any unreceived items. Cancel PO : cancels the open purchase order. For open POs only. Close PO : changes the purchase order quantities to show as fully received. For partially received POs only. Disassociate PO : unlinks the purchase order from this service request. Note: The same window displays when you delete or decline a package, or cancel the order, when it has a line on an open PO. Note: Each choice needs its access right: Service Request - Complete PO/PO Items Linked to SR, Service Request - Cancel PO/PO Items Linked to SR, Service Request - Disassociate PO/PO Items Linked to SR, and for Close PO both Service Request - Close PO/PO Items Linked to SR and Purchase Orders - Close PO. Users without any of these rights see a message to contact the system administrator, and the line is not deleted."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#view-item-details-from-the-order", "t": "View item details from the order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Hover to the left of a line item and select the blue \"i\" to see the item's full inventory information. See View item details and time logs above."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#enter-dot-numbers", "t": "Enter DOT numbers", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Double-click the tire line item and select the DOT number icon . The Add/Edit DoT Number icon also shows when you hover to the left of a tire line. In Edit DoT Numbers , enter the DOT number for each tire. Use the copy buttons to copy the previous value, or to copy the first value to all tires. If your store uses TireMetrix TRP, select Search Base DOT# to pick from the base DOT numbers TireMetrix suggests, then enter the 4-digit date code. If the tire was made at more than one plant, you are reminded to use the correct base DOT number. If your store requires valid DOT numbers, Done is blocked with \"You must enter a valid DOT Number to continue.\" until the number is valid. Note: Changing DOT numbers on a closed order needs the Service Request - Change DoT Numbers access right."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#cancel-an-order", "t": "Cancel an order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": "Select Cancel Order . You are asked \"Are you sure you want to cancel this Service Request?\" If the order has a payment or deposit applied: Users with the Cancel Orders with Applied Payments access right are warned that canceling may require a refund to the customer, and can continue. Everyone else sees that the order cannot be canceled and should contact a supervisor. If the order has a line on an open purchase order, the Associated PO window displays. See Delete a line above."}, {"u": "creating-a-service-request.html#more-service-request-tools", "t": "More service request tools", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Creating a service request", "x": ": gives a quote without leaving the service request. Print : prints the service request. ... (next to Save ): opens Tire Adjustments , Retreads , Change Inv. Date and View Audit History . View Audit History shows who opened, saved and closed the order, and when discounts were added or removed. : shows packages in tab view, list view or service request view. Tip: When you hover in the service request, anything that shows a hand, an underline or blue text has more functionality under your cursor."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html", "t": "Electronic Payments", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "Use electronic payments to take card payments on Service Requests, Customer Deposits, and Receipts On Account. A store takes card payments through one of two processors, depending on how the store is set up: 1stMile (also called Merchant Partners) or iPOSPays. A store uses one or the other, not both. Card payments work the same way on all three order types. The differences between the processors are described below."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#what-differs-between-the-two-processors", "t": "What differs between the two processors", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "1stMile : The 1stMile window opens on your computer to take the card. When the store is set up for it, 1stMile also handles checks, plus Text-to-Pay and Cards on File. iPOSPays : A standalone card terminal takes the card. The terminal doesn't need to be connected to your computer. A \"Connecting to credit card terminal...\" message shows while TireWorks HD waits on the terminal. iPOSPays offers cash discounting. It doesn't offer Text-to-Pay, Cards on File, or electronic check sales."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#select-a-credit-card-terminal-ipospays", "t": "Select a credit card terminal (iPOSPays)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "When you log in at a store that uses iPOSPays, the Credit Card Terminals window asks you to \"Select credit card terminal for this session:\". Choose the terminal at your counter. To skip this prompt the next time you log in to this location, check Do not ask again . This checkbox only shows for users with the Access Right Credit Card Terminal \"Do Not Ask Again\" Selection. Select Done ."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#change-your-credit-card-terminal", "t": "Change your credit card terminal", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "Go to TireWorks; My Preferences , and open the Credit Card Terminal tab. Pick a new terminal from Credit Card Terminal Name , or clear Do Not Ask Again On Location Selection . Select Test Status to confirm the terminal is online. Note: Managers add terminals in Location Setup; Credit Card Terminals , with a Terminal Name, Terminal Profile Number (TPN), and Authorization Key."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#take-a-card-payment", "t": "Take a card payment", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "In Add Payment , select Credit Card in Payment Type . Enter the Payment Amount . Select Apply . Complete the card payment. 1stMile : Complete the card in the 1stMile window. iPOSPays : The customer taps, inserts, or swipes on the terminal. Note: With 1stMile, when the store is set up for checks, choosing Check opens the 1stMile Check Sale screen. Note: With iPOSPays, if cash discounting is turned on for your store and the customer chooses cash on the terminal, the store's cash discount is added to the Service Request. Cash discounting isn't allowed on Customer Deposits or Receipts On Account. On those, retry and don't pick the cash option."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#if-an-electronic-payment-fails", "t": "If an electronic payment fails", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "A failed card charge shows \"Credit Card NOT charged!!\" and asks \"Do you want to enter a Credit Card transaction manually?\" Yes : Type in the card details for a charge that was run another way. No : Go back and try again. A failed check shows \"Check sale NOT processed!!!\" and offers to enter the check manually. Note: The manual option only shows for users with the Access Right Payments - Manual Credit Card. Without it, you're told you don't have access and returned to the payment screen."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#save-a-card-on-file-1stmile", "t": "Save a card on file (1stMile)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "When 1stMile asks \"Tokenize this card?\", answer Yes to save the card to the bill-to customer. Saved cards show on the customer's Cards On File tab, with the Card Number, Card Type, and Security Token. Important: To remove a saved card, hover over the card, select the Delete icon, and confirm. This can't be undone."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#charge-a-saved-card-1stmile", "t": "Charge a saved card (1stMile)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "In Payment Type , choose Credit Card on File . Select the card from the list. Note: Credit Card on File only shows when the bill-to customer has a saved card. Note: If the charge fails, \"Credit Card on File NOT charged!!\" returns you to the payment screen. There's no manual option for a saved card."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#send-a-text-to-pay-link-1stmile", "t": "Send a Text-to-Pay link (1stMile)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "On a saved Service Request, select the Text To Pay icon next to Add Payment . Under Create New PayLink , enter the Amount . It can't be more than the remaining balance. Enter the Phone . The customer's default text-enabled contact fills in first. You can send to another number. Select Send . The TextToPay Links list shows each link's Amount and Status. From the list, you can use these buttons: Delete : Cancels the link. Resend : Sends the link again. Accept : Applies a paid link to the order. Note: Paid links are checked about every five minutes. The store gets a text when a customer pays, and the Service Request list shows a partially or fully paid icon."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#voids-refunds-and-reversals", "t": "Voids, Refunds, and Reversals", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "Removing a card payment : Within about 8 minutes, the payment is voided. After that, it's refunded to the card. Reversals (Return Order) : Your store may ask \"Would you like this reversal to refund the customer's credit card?\" Yes refunds the card. No leaves the card alone (\"Do not refund the card\"). Refund the customer another way if needed. Receipts On Account : Removing a card payment asks you to confirm the void at your processor. Customer Deposits : Reversing a deposit paid by card voids or refunds the card and shows the refunded amount and authorization number. Refund Unused Amount : On a partly used deposit, add the refund payments, then select Save ."}, {"u": "electronic-payments.html#when-store-account-doesn-t-show", "t": "When Store Account doesn't show", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Electronic Payments", "x": "The Store Account payment type is hidden when: The customer is a business customer with a $0 credit limit ( Customer Maintenance , General tab). The customer is past due. Cash, Credit Card, Credit Card on File, Check, and Customer Deposits stay available."}, {"u": "customer-approval.html", "t": "Customer Approval", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Approval", "x": "Use Customer Approval to have the customer authorize a Service Request before you save, print, or invoice it at the order states your company chose. The customer can sign in the store, or you can record how they approved when they aren't there."}, {"u": "customer-approval.html#set-up-customer-approval", "t": "Set up Customer Approval", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Approval", "x": "Go to Manage; Location Setup; Locations , and open the General tab. Check Signature Capture to turn Customer Approval on for the store. Go to Manage; Company Setup; Company , and open the Signature Capture tab. Move each order state that should ask for approval from All SR Order States to Enabled SR Order States with the > button. Use < to remove a state. Note: Both parts of the setup are needed. If the store box is checked but no order states are listed, the Customer Approval prompt never appears."}, {"u": "customer-approval.html#get-the-customer-s-approval", "t": "Get the customer's approval", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Approval", "x": "When you save, print, or invoice at a listed order state, the Customer Approval prompt asks \"Approve via signature?\" Choose one of these options: OK : The customer signs on the signature pad, and you select Save , or Clear to start over. If your store's credit card terminal supports signatures, the customer signs on the terminal instead. Customer Not Present : Use this when the customer isn't in the store. At Select Customer Approval Reason , choose how the customer approved in Select Approval Reason . Complete Authorized By , Authorized Contact , and Comments/Notes as needed, then select Save . Text To Authorize : Texts the customer a link. Pick the customer's cell number in Authorized Contact and select Send . The customer views the Service Request on their phone and signs there. Not Now : Closes the prompt without approving. The order doesn't finish saving or invoicing. Note: Customer Not Present covers only the current session on that order. It isn't offered at invoicing when Get Approval is turned on and Invoice is a listed order state. Note: Text To Authorize shows only when the System Setting \"Merchant Partners - Text to Authorize Enabled\" is on."}, {"u": "customer-approval.html#when-the-customer-is-asked-to-sign-again", "t": "When the customer is asked to sign again", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Approval", "x": "Once signed, the order doesn't ask again unless the total goes above the amount the customer signed for. A lower total doesn't ask again. Neither does a higher total caused only by removing a discount that was already on the signed order. Reprinting an invoice that already printed doesn't ask for a signature."}, {"u": "customer-approval.html#record-approval-for-added-work-get-approval", "t": "Record approval for added work (Get Approval)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Approval", "x": "Stores with Get Approval turned on see a Get Approval button on the Service Request. Use it to record how the customer approved added work. Select Get Approval . Complete the Select Customer Approval Reason window, including Additional Service and Additional Amount . Select Save . Note: When the total changes after the estimate, the order can also ask for an approval reason on save. The first time, it may ask \"Is $[total] the final initial estimate?\""}, {"u": "customer-approval.html#approval-column-on-the-home-screen", "t": "Approval column on the Home screen", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Approval", "x": "The Approval column on the Service Request tab shows Text To Authorize links only: Clock : \"Pending Customer Action for Approval\". Check mark : The customer signed the link. Blank : No link was sent. Note: A phone, email, or Customer Not Present approval doesn't change this column. You also get a text message in the store's text message portal when the customer signs."}, {"u": "order-prompts.html", "t": "Order Prompts", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Order Prompts", "x": "Use Order Prompts to have TireWorks HD ask your own questions on a Quick Quote, Appointment, or Service Request. You choose the order states and actions that ask each question, the answer type, and whether an answer is required."}, {"u": "order-prompts.html#set-up-an-order-prompt", "t": "Set up an order prompt", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Order Prompts", "x": "Before you start: You need the Access Right \"Manage - Order Prompts\". Go to Manage; Location Setup; Order Prompts . Select Add Prompt . Under Order States , check each state that should ask the question: Quick Quote, Appointment, Open, Estimate, Work Order, Invoice, Declined, or Cancelled. For each checked state, pick Prompt When : Order is Saved , Customer is Assigned to the Order , or Vehicle is Assigned to the Order . Declined and Cancelled always ask when the order is saved. In Required: , pick the first state where an answer is required, or Not Required . That state and every state after it require an answer. Under Question and Answers , enter the Question: . Pick the Answer Type: : Alphanumeric, True False, List With Single Select, or List With Multi Select. For a list, enter each choice in Answer: and select Add . Select Done , or Add Another to start the next prompt. Answer Yes to \"Do you want to make the prompt Active?\" to start using it. Save the screen. Tip: Use Copy Order Prompts to copy saved prompts to other stores. Important: Changing the answer type clears the answers you already entered for that prompt."}, {"u": "order-prompts.html#answer-prompts-on-an-order", "t": "Answer prompts on an order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Order Prompts", "x": "When a prompt's state and action are reached, the Answer the following questions window opens. Answer each question. Select Done . A * marks a required prompt. You can't continue until every required prompt is answered. Tip: Check Show Previous Prompts to see questions from earlier order states. Note: The System Setting \"Order Prompts - Show Previous Prompts by Default\" makes Show Previous Prompts checked each time the window opens."}, {"u": "order-prompts.html#order-validation-and-prompts-window", "t": "Order Validation and Prompts window", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Order Prompts", "x": "When you save or invoice an order, the Order Validation and Prompts window lists open validations, and any unanswered prompts under Prompts . Answer : Select it next to a prompt to answer that prompt. Show Prompts : Review or change prompt answers, even when none are pending. Note: An order with an unanswered required prompt can't be saved or invoiced."}, {"u": "customer-communication-texting.html", "t": "Customer Communication (Texting)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Communication (Texting)", "x": "Use two-way texting to text customers from TireWorks HD. Customers can reply to your texts, and their replies come back into TireWorks HD. Every text, email, and call note for a customer is kept together in Customer Communication."}, {"u": "customer-communication-texting.html#contacts-that-can-receive-texts", "t": "Contacts that can receive texts", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Communication (Texting)", "x": "You can text a customer at any contact with Contact Type Text , or Contact Type Phone or Phone 2 with Phone Type Cell . To add one, enter the number in the customer's Contact Info and select Add . Note: Cell Provider isn't needed for two-way texting and is hidden when two-way texting is on. It only shows for stores still set up for the older one-way (email-to-text) method."}, {"u": "customer-communication-texting.html#sms-hub-home-screen", "t": "SMS Hub (Home screen)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Communication (Texting)", "x": "The SMS Hub icon sits at the top right of the Home screen. A red balloon shows the number of unread messages. Over 99 shows \"99+\". New messages are checked about every 60 seconds by default. Select the SMS Hub icon to open the SMS list of unread messages. Each message shows the customer name (or \"Anonymous\" if the number isn't on file), phone number, time, vehicle, and message. From the list, you can: Order icon : Opens that order. Read icon : Marks the message with Mark as Read or Mark as Unread . Double-click a message : Opens the conversation so you can reply. Note: The SMS Hub also receives alerts from TireWorks HD itself, such as a new appointment or quote booked online, auto-replenishment results, a failed TCS Inspect submission, or a customer's remote authorization. Note: The SMS Hub isn't available while your session is locked."}, {"u": "customer-communication-texting.html#send-a-text", "t": "Send a text", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Communication (Texting)", "x": "Open the conversation from one of these places: On a Service Request, select Send Text (the Customer Texts icon). A red count shows unread replies. On the Home screen Service Request and Quick Quote lists, hover over an order and select the Customer Texts icon. From the Appointment and Quick Quote windows. Choose the number from the drop-down under the customer name. From a Service Request, the list defaults to the primary contact of the member on the order and shows only that member's numbers, plus any address contacts marked Cell. Type the message. Messages can be up to 1600 characters. The counter below the box shows the characters used. Select Send . Note: Emojis sent by customers display in the conversation. Tip: Use Find at the top of the conversation to search the messages."}, {"u": "customer-communication-texting.html#set-up-canned-messages", "t": "Set up canned messages", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Communication (Texting)", "x": "Go to Manage; Company Setup; Canned Text Messages . Enter a Message Code , Message Title , Message , and Message Category . Use Apply To... to choose which locations can use the message."}, {"u": "customer-communication-texting.html#use-canned-messages-and-placeholders", "t": "Use canned messages and placeholders", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Communication (Texting)", "x": "To use a canned message, open Canned Messages on the left of the text window and double-click a message, or pick one from Quick Add Template . Most Popular lists the 10 most used messages at your store. Placeholders fill in customer, order, vehicle, and store details for you. They work in typed messages and in canned messages. To add one, open Placeholder on the right and double-click one, or type # to see suggestions. Examples include #CustFirstName, #OrderId, #OrderTotal, #VehicleDesc, #LocationPhone, #InspLiveFeed, #PromiseDT (promise date and time), and #ApptDateTime (earliest appointment date and time on the order). Note: Use of canned messages and placeholders is controlled by the Canned Text Messages access rights."}, {"u": "customer-communication-texting.html#customer-communication-screen", "t": "Customer Communication screen", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Customer Communication (Texting)", "x": "Use the Customer Communication screen to see a customer's messages and call notes in one place. Open it from the Communication button on a Service Request, the View Customer Communication icon on the Home screen lists, or the Communication tab in Customer Maintenance. The list shows emails, call notes, texts, Text-to-Pay, and Text-to-Auth messages, with Status, Location, Type, Direction, Date, Reference, Contact, and Subject/Message. Filters : Filter the list with Dates (Last 7 Days by default), Include All Locations , the type check boxes, Show , and Look For . Show : Limits the list to InBound (Internal), OutBound (Internal), Inbound (External), or Outbound (External). Internal is a message sent or received through TireWorks HD. External is a message from your Cinch messaging service, if your company uses Cinch. Magnifier : Opens a message so you can read it. The message is then marked as read. Call Note : Enter a note and select Save . Send Text : Type a message, choose the number in To , and select Send Text ."}, {"u": "tcs-inspect.html", "t": "TCS Inspect", "p": "Section 2: Sales › TCS Inspect", "x": "Use TCS Inspect, the tablet inspection app, to bring vehicle inspections into TireWorks HD. There you can link them to orders, review photos and videos, and send the results to the customer. Before you start: TCS Inspect setup is done with TCS and is found at Manage; Company Setup; TCS Inspect Configuration ."}, {"u": "tcs-inspect.html#inspections-tab-home-screen", "t": "Inspections tab (Home screen)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › TCS Inspect", "x": "The Inspections tab lists inspections for the selected Dates , with Id#, Date Created, Procedure, Vehicle, Mileage, and Linked Order. Show Unlinked Inspections Only : Shows inspections not yet attached to an order. Depending on your store's setup, the tab may be highlighted when unlinked inspections are waiting. Filter : Searches by Id, vehicle name, or order Id. View Inspection : Opens the selected inspection. You can also double-click an inspection to open it."}, {"u": "tcs-inspect.html#link-an-inspection-to-an-order", "t": "Link an inspection to an order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › TCS Inspect", "x": "On the Inspections tab, select Link To Service Request . The Link TCS Inspection window lists orders at your store for the same VIN. Select the order, then select Link . Select Yes to confirm. Tip: To start a new order instead, select Create a new Service Request . The VIN and mileage carry over. Note: You can also link from a vehicle's Inspections tab inside a Service Request. There, Link To Service Request links to that order. Save the order first. Select Open Linked Service Request to open the order, or Unlink from Service Request to remove the link. Note: An inspection can only be linked to one order. Copying a Service Request doesn't copy its inspections."}, {"u": "tcs-inspect.html#inspections-on-the-service-request", "t": "Inspections on the Service Request", "p": "Section 2: Sales › TCS Inspect", "x": "On the Home screen Service Request list, a TCS Inspect icon with a red count shows inspections on that order that haven't been viewed yet. The count clears once the inspection is opened. On the Service Request, select the TCS Inspect icon to see TCS Inspect Report(s) , then select one to open it. To copy the customer's live feed link, select Copy TCS Inspect Live Feed Url . TCS Inspect Recommendations shows the recommended items from the inspection that can be added to the order. Note: Technicians can submit inspections while the order is open in TireWorks HD. Reopen the order to see the new data."}, {"u": "tcs-inspect.html#inspection-detail", "t": "Inspection detail", "p": "Section 2: Sales › TCS Inspect", "x": "The header shows Inspection Id, Procedure, Order Id, Created At, Inspection Started, Inspection Submitted, Total Inspection Time, Vehicle, VIN, Mileage, Marked 'All Okay', App Type, License, State, and Related Inspections. Note: A warning icon means the vehicle information may have changed since the inspection. The services list shows each service with Comments, Active, Media, and Detail. Media : Select the icon to view all photos and videos for that service. Scroll to see each one. View Tire Data Attributes and View Brake Data Attributes : Show the Tire Measurements and Brakes Measurements. Use the buttons at the bottom of the window to share the inspection: Print : Prints the inspection report. Email : Emails the inspection report. Send Text : Opens a text with the inspection report link. Text Live Feed URL : Opens a text with the customer's live feed link. The inspection must be linked to an order that has a live feed."}, {"u": "tcs-inspect.html#print-the-inspection-with-the-invoice", "t": "Print the inspection with the invoice", "p": "Section 2: Sales › TCS Inspect", "x": "To print the inspection report automatically when the order is invoiced, set up a document at Manage; Company Setup; Auto Print Documents with Document Source Type set to Inspection . Every inspection linked to the order then prints along with the invoice."}, {"u": "catalogs.html", "t": "Catalogs", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Catalogs", "x": "Parts, labor, vehicle, and tire fitment data come from the catalog your store is set up to use. TCS sets up the catalog for each store. What you see on the F1, F2, F4, and F6 screens and on the vehicle screens depends on that catalog. See Catalog Updates for how catalog data is kept current."}, {"u": "catalogs.html#epicor-ise", "t": "Epicor ISE", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Catalogs", "x": "If your store uses Epicor ISE, parts and labor searches and package resolution use Epicor's online service. Vehicle Conditions : Epicor may ask questions about the vehicle (for example, engine or transmission details) before it returns parts or labor. The Vehicle Conditions window lists each question with its answers in a list. No answer is picked for you. Answer each question. Select Done . The window can't be closed with Esc or the X until the questions are answered. Note: The same question can come up more than once, because Epicor asks it separately for Parts, Labor, FSM, and Vehicle Specs. The window shows which of these it's asking for. Catalog Job packages : A package can hold a Catalog Job, which is one Epicor job that includes all the parts and labor for the service. These packages resolve in F2 like any other catalog package. Note: Catalog Job packages can only be used at Epicor ISE stores. Anywhere else, you see \"This package has a Catalog Job item type and cannot be used in non-ISE enabled locations. Please select another package.\" F2 pricing : Prices are color-coded. White : Your store's own inventory price, for parts you stock. Yellow : Vendor pricing. Real-time supplier pricing (live supplier cost) and your customer pricing are also told apart by color. Suppliers : Supplier names come from Epicor ISE. When a supplier has stock at another of its locations, each location is listed on its own line with its quantity. The Supplier Name column shows \"[Seller Name] - [Alt. Location Name]\"."}, {"u": "catalogs.html#missing-catalog-descriptions", "t": "Missing catalog descriptions", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Catalogs", "x": "A catalog part or labor item in a package needs catalog descriptions so the catalog can be searched. If a package you pick in F2 has catalog items with none set up, you're asked whether to add the package using the default part and labor items instead. Yes : Adds the package with the default items. No : Cancels. A message explains how to fix the package: in Manage; Company Setup; Packages , select the catalog part or labor item, then select Maintain List... under Catalog Descriptions ."}, {"u": "catalogs.html#tireguide", "t": "TireGuide", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Catalogs", "x": "TireGuide provides tire fitment only. If your store uses TireGuide: Adding a vehicle : The fields are Year, Make, Model, and Option. Option is the trim or submodel, not the engine. Vehicle lookup : To look up by plate and state, or by VIN, use the CARFAX QuickVin button. The VIN Lookup button isn't shown. Existing vehicles : Vehicles created under another catalog may need to be opened, updated, and saved again after a store switches to TireGuide. Vehicle information : The Oil Settings , Conditions , and Vin Details tabs aren't shown. Tire fitments show on the Tire Fitment Details tab. Tire fitments : Fitments from TireGuide are saved to the vehicle and used by F1 searches the same way as other catalogs. F4 and F6 : F4 Diagnosticator and F6 FSM aren't shown. F2 : There are no Parts or Labor tabs. Packages that contain catalog parts or catalog labor are left out of F2 package results."}, {"u": "catalogs.html#add-a-vehicle-during-a-search", "t": "Add a vehicle during a search", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Catalogs", "x": "The F1, F2, and F3 screens have an Add Vehicle button. Use it to add a vehicle to the order without closing the search. Fitment is available right away. The button isn't shown on carry-out orders. To start a quote from a vehicle, select Add Vehicle below Quick Tire Search on the Home screen. Enter a plate or VIN. A Quick Quote opens with that vehicle, and F1 searches the first tire fitment. Note: If the plate or VIN matches an existing customer, you're asked whether to use that customer and vehicle, so you don't create a duplicate. Note: Catalog setup is done by TCS. Contact TCS Support if your store's catalog needs to change."}, {"u": "tire-package-fees-road-hazard-nitrogen-and-tire-disposal.html", "t": "Tire Package Fees (Road Hazard, Nitrogen and Tire Disposal)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Tire Package Fees (Road Hazard, Nitrogen and Tire Disposal)", "x": "Use tire package fees to add Road Hazard, Nitrogen, and Tire Disposal to tire packages, or to record that the customer declined them. Each fee is set up per store and only appears when it's turned on for that store."}, {"u": "tire-package-fees-road-hazard-nitrogen-and-tire-disposal.html#add-or-decline-a-fee-on-an-order", "t": "Add or decline a fee on an order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Tire Package Fees (Road Hazard, Nitrogen and Tire Disposal)", "x": "Service Requests, Quick Quotes, and Appointments show these buttons on a package that holds a tire: Add RH / Decline RH : Road Hazard. Add N2 / Decline N2 : Nitrogen. Add DISP / Decline DISP : Tire Disposal, if your store uses it. Add adds the store's fee item at its price for the order's price level. Decline adds the store's declined item at $0.00. Decline buttons show only when the store tracks declines for that fee. Note: The buttons are hidden once the order is completed, and on Goodyear orders. Tire Disposal buttons are also hidden on any special program order, such as TreadNet."}, {"u": "tire-package-fees-road-hazard-nitrogen-and-tire-disposal.html#add-fees-from-the-f1-tire-quote-window", "t": "Add fees from the F1 Tire Quote window", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Tire Package Fees (Road Hazard, Nitrogen and Tire Disposal)", "x": "On Tire Quote , Include Road Hazard? , Include Nitrogen? , and Include Tire Disposal? add the fee items to packages added from Tire Quote. Nitrogen and Tire Disposal show only when set up for the store. Note: Whether each box starts checked depends on your store's System Settings, set separately for Quick Quotes and Appointments and for Service Requests."}, {"u": "tire-package-fees-road-hazard-nitrogen-and-tire-disposal.html#order-validation-for-tire-package-fees", "t": "Order Validation for tire package fees", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Tire Package Fees (Road Hazard, Nitrogen and Tire Disposal)", "x": "Order Validation can warn or block when a tire package has neither the fee nor the declined item. Set Road Hazard , Nitrogen , and Tire Disposal to Ignore , Warn , or Block in Manage; Location Setup; Order Validation . See Order Validation . When validation stops an order, select Fix to use Add Road Hazard / Decline Road Hazard , Add Nitrogen / Decline Nitrogen , or Add Tire Disposal / Decline Tire Disposal . Note: Road Hazard and Nitrogen are only checked when the store tracks declines for that fee, and they aren't checked on Goodyear orders. Tire Disposal isn't checked on any special program order."}, {"u": "tire-package-fees-road-hazard-nitrogen-and-tire-disposal.html#set-up-tire-package-fees", "t": "Set up tire package fees", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Tire Package Fees (Road Hazard, Nitrogen and Tire Disposal)", "x": "Go to Manage; Company Setup; Other Fees & Charges . The window has Shop Fees , Road Hazard , Nitrogen , and Tire Disposal tabs. On the fee's tab, select a store from the list. Under Configuration , check RH Active , N2 Active , or Tire Disposal Active to turn the fee on for the store. Set the other options as needed: Automatically Add ... : Adds the fee on its own. Taxable : Marks the fee as taxable. Use Inventory Tree Mapping : Limits the fee to chosen manufacturers, sub manufacturers, or classes. Track Declined ... : Records declines using the Declined Item you pick. Create Item makes a new item without leaving the window. In the items grid, select Add New RH Setting , Add New Nitrogen Setting , or Add New DISP Setting to add one setting per price level. Set the SKU Code , a fixed price or a percent of the tire price with Max , Min , and Rounding Cut Off , and the GL Account . Select Save . Tip: To reuse a finished setup, select Copy Road Hazard Settings (or the Nitrogen, Tire Disposal, or Shop Fee copy button), pick the stores, and select Copy . Check Overwrite existing metrics at destinations to replace setups those stores already have. Note: Tire Disposal is turned on through TCS Support. Until then, its tab, buttons, and checkbox don't appear."}, {"u": "tire-package-fees-road-hazard-nitrogen-and-tire-disposal.html#manage-packages", "t": "Manage packages", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Tire Package Fees (Road Hazard, Nitrogen and Tire Disposal)", "x": "Use Manage; Company Setup; Packages to set up the tire and service packages used on orders. Use Look For to find a package by code or name. Show Inactive Packages : Lists inactive packages too. New packages start out Active. Line Item Type : Sets each package item's type, such as a stock item, a Catalog Part, Catalog Labor, or, at Epicor ISE stores, a Catalog Job. Maintain List... : For catalog items, found under Catalog Descriptions . Picks what the catalog should search for. A Catalog Job item holds one job, found by Job Description, Job Code, or Job Category. Program Product Codes... : Sets the Product Code for each special program, plus a Cost Surcharge Code and Quantity Surcharge Code for surcharges. Clone : Copies the selected package as a new package. Note: A package can't be deleted if it's the Default package, if it's used as an installation package, or if open orders use it. Make it inactive instead."}, {"u": "parts-cores.html", "t": "Parts Cores", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Parts Cores", "x": "Use Parts Cores to link an item to a core item so the core can be added to orders with it. A core is the returnable part (for example, an old battery) that carries a core charge. Before you start: Parts Cores is turned on with the System Setting \"Parts Core - Active\". Until then, the Core tabs described here don't appear."}, {"u": "parts-cores.html#set-up-an-item-s-core", "t": "Set up an item's core", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Parts Cores", "x": "Go to Manage; Inventory; Manage Inventory . Select the item, then select the Core tab. Choose a Core Type : Item not a Core : No core. The rest of the tab stays inactive. Item is a Core : This item is a core item and can be linked to other items. Item has a Core : This item carries a core charge. For Item has a Core , pick one option under Core Selection : Create Core based on this item : Enter the Core Cost . A new core item is created with the same part number plus \"-C\". Select Core item : Search (at least four characters) for an existing item marked Item is a Core . Choose how the core is handled when this item goes on an order, separately for Customer Transactions and Vendor Transactions : Never (Manually Add) : The core is only added if you add it yourself. Prompt User : You're asked each time. Always Add : The core is added automatically. Select Save . You see \"Core data saved successfully\". Note: An item that's linked as the core of other items can't be changed away from Item is a Core until it's removed from those items. Deleting a linked item asks you to confirm breaking its core links. Note: If your store uses Epicor ISE, adding a catalog part that has a core cost creates the core item for you when one doesn't already exist."}, {"u": "parts-cores.html#add-an-item-with-a-core-to-an-order", "t": "Add an item with a core to an order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Parts Cores", "x": "If the item is set to Prompt User , you see: \"SKU '[item]' has an associated Core '[core]' with a Core Charge of '[amount]'. Do you want to add that Core also to the transaction?\" Select Yes to add the core at the same quantity as the item. Core credits : If your store uses them, adding a core item also adds a matching negative-quantity line, \"Core: [description] -CREDIT\", at the same price. This lets the store charge the core's tax even when the old part is returned. Depending on your store's settings, the credit line may be tax exempt."}, {"u": "parts-cores.html#return-or-put-away-unsold-cores", "t": "Return or put away unsold cores", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Parts Cores", "x": "On the Home screen, go to Unsold Purchases , and open the Unsold Cores tab. The tab lists core items with quantity still available. Select cores and use Create Return or Put Away , the same way as on the Unsold Purchases Items tab. See Unsold Purchases . Note: New core items get their SKU Type, inventory tree location, and cost field from the store's Parts Core System Settings, or from the parent item when those aren't set. These are normally set by TCS."}, {"u": "goodyear-national-account-p-r-secondary-supply-or-government.html", "t": "Goodyear National Account, P&R, Secondary Supply or Government Processing", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Goodyear National Account, P&R, Secondary Supply or Government Processing", "x": "Use Goodyear National Account processing to submit Goodyear transactions directly to the manufacturer automatically, while the sale stays on the customer's account for easy tracking of customer and vehicle data. The same process covers the P&R, Secondary Supply, and Government special programs. Note: For Bridgestone Firestone national accounts, see Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts (TreadNet) ."}, {"u": "goodyear-national-account-p-r-secondary-supply-or-government.html#create-a-goodyear-national-account-order", "t": "Create a Goodyear National Account order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Goodyear National Account, P&R, Secondary Supply or Government Processing", "x": "Start a new Service Request and continue as you would for any service request. If the customer was previously invoiced as a national account, a window asks you to select the customer's special program. If the program is correct, select Done . If the program is wrong, select the right program, then select Done . To use no program, select Cancel . The program defaults to None. Select the vehicle, then select Done . By default, a Goodyear National Account order uses Goodyear NA as the special program. The price level defaults to the desired price level, and tax detail and tire tax change to exempt. If this is the customer's first National Account order, select Goodyear NA in the header record FIRST. The Goodyear National Account Selector opens. Verify the Document Type is correct. It defaults based on the Special Program selected, and the account search uses the Document Type you select. Verify the Vehicle type , and change it from the drop-down if needed. Enter the National Account name or customer code in Look For . In In , select Customer Name or Customer Code . Select Search . Select the National Account. To leave without choosing an account, close the window with the X. A warning explains that a Goodyear Special Program order needs a National Account. Select OK to close and set the Special Program back to None, or Cancel to go back to the selector. Select the Goodyear icon that now shows on the service request. Everything in this window is stored with the customer's information and filled in each time a service request is created. Some requirements are specific to the order and need to be filled in on each new service request."}, {"u": "goodyear-national-account-p-r-secondary-supply-or-government.html#complete-the-goodyear-tabs", "t": "Complete the Goodyear tabs", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Goodyear National Account, P&R, Secondary Supply or Government Processing", "x": "General tab : Shows customer information, billing account information, Goodyear Customer Code, NonSig, and National Account Name. For the Secondary Supply special program, the General tab has a requirement: At Goodyear Customer Code (Ship-To) , select the Assign icon. Enter the customer name or store number, if applicable. Select the customer. The Ship-To field fills in. Select Done . Note: You can change National Account information by selecting any of the underlined fields. Requirements tab : Lists all the information required for a successful submission. Verify the Document and Vehicle Type . Fill in the Requirement Values . Letters MUST be upper case. The Mask column shows the field format required. Verify that the Status column shows all green check marks. Select Done . Additional Data tab : Holds additional data that isn't required and generally isn't needed. If required data is missing, a red X shows on the tab. For the P&R special program, the Additional Data tab needs more data: Select the Manufacturer default. At PR Code , select the Lookup icon. Verify the Manufacturer and enter the dealership name. Select Lookup . Select the correct dealership, then select Done . The Customer Code , Name , and NonSig number fill in on the tab and are copied into Ship-to on the General tab. For the Government special program, the Additional Data tab needs more data: Select the proper document indicator, then select Done . The red X is replaced with a green check mark."}, {"u": "goodyear-national-account-p-r-secondary-supply-or-government.html#add-items-to-a-goodyear-order", "t": "Add items to a Goodyear order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Goodyear National Account, P&R, Secondary Supply or Government Processing", "x": "Add items to the service request as needed, following these rules. Important: Tires : Change the tire package to a Goodyear Passenger, Light Truck, or Commercial tire package, either on the quote screen or in Add Items, before adding it to the service request. Important: Packages : Select a GY package, if applicable, so the order gets proper credit from the manufacturer. GY Tire Packages : When added, show an extra column with the Goodyear Product Number on each line of the package, matched to the in-house item numbers. Tire Tax : Blank, and not submitted to the manufacturer. Road Hazard : For order validation, every order must have an approve or a decline to process. Road Hazard is also skipped for manufacturer processing. All other line items : Must have a GY reference number. If one is missing, select the product column of that row and fill it in. GY Service Packages : When added, also show an extra column with the Goodyear Product Number on each line of the package, matched to the in-house item numbers. All line items : Must have a GY reference number. If one is missing, select the product column of that row and fill it in. Note: Oil packages must have the correct GY product code assigned to the additional oil surcharge (1/2 Quart or Full Quart). Individual items : GY individual item numbers aren't used. Use the in-house item number so inventory is relieved. Every in-house item number is referenced to a Goodyear Product Number. All line items : Must have a GY reference number. If one is missing, select the product column of that row and fill it in."}, {"u": "goodyear-national-account-p-r-secondary-supply-or-government.html#validate-and-invoice-a-goodyear-order", "t": "Validate and invoice a Goodyear order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Goodyear National Account, P&R, Secondary Supply or Government Processing", "x": "Select Validate TireHQ . This MUST be done before you accept payment. If the order has everything required for processing, a message confirms the validation succeeded. If the order is missing requirements, a message directs you to the items that need correcting. After a successful validation, select the payment type. Apply the payment. Select Done . The amount due shows $0. Continue when prompted, after you verify the $0 balance due. The invoice displays for printing or emailing. At invoicing, the order is submitted to the manufacturer automatically. Note: Government accounts with service use 000000000 as the GY product code to bypass TireHQ submission."}, {"u": "goodyear-national-account-p-r-secondary-supply-or-government.html#return-a-goodyear-national-account-order", "t": "Return a Goodyear National Account order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Goodyear National Account, P&R, Secondary Supply or Government Processing", "x": "Goodyear National Account returns work the same way as a sale, with a few exceptions. Create a sales order as you would for a new sale. BEFORE you select the Goodyear icon , add the items being returned. Enter a negative quantity. Don't enter negative dollar amounts. Open the Goodyear icon and fill in all tabs for the National Account Type selected. The Returns tab only shows when the order has a negative quantity. Fill in the Returns tab. Use the small arrows to change date segments, or the large arrow to pick a date from the calendar. Select WILL-CALL/PICKUP , or any ship method that doesn't involve shipment manager. Add the Reference Document Number in the order comments. Select Process to invoice the return."}, {"u": "bridgestone-firestone-national-accounts-treadnet.html", "t": "Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts (TreadNet)", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts (TreadNet)", "x": "Use Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts to send an order's delivery receipt (DR) to Bridgestone's TreadNet system. If your store is set up for it, TireWorks HD builds the DR, sends it to TreadNet, then brings the TreadNet invoice back into TireWorks HD. This works like Goodyear National Accounts, but with its own screens."}, {"u": "bridgestone-firestone-national-accounts-treadnet.html#start-a-national-account-order", "t": "Start a national account order", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts (TreadNet)", "x": "Create the service request as usual. Select the Bridgestone special program for the customer. When the order is linked to a TreadNet program, the TreadNet button shows above the packages and line items. Select TreadNet to open Bridgestone Firestone National Account . If no fleet or dealer is assigned yet, the Bridgestone Firestone National Account Selector opens. Answer the Billed Customer Questions : Is this a Dealer-to-Dealer transaction? Is this Delivery Receipt for a customer billed locally? Does this Delivery Receipt contains an Off-The-Road (OTR) tire(s) or service(s)? Was this a tire(s) only sale? Was the service done on specific vehicle? The answers set the DR Type. Changing an answer later restarts the delivery receipt. Search by Fleet Id (or Dealer Id ), Name , Address , or City . Select the account, then select Done ."}, {"u": "bridgestone-firestone-national-accounts-treadnet.html#requirements-submission-and-status-tabs", "t": "Requirements, Submission, and Status tabs", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts (TreadNet)", "x": "General : Shows the Customer Name, Customer Id, and DR Type. Select the fleet link to change it. Requirements : Lists what TreadNet needs for this fleet and DR Type. Required items are marked with *, and the Validation and Status columns show what's still missing. Some requirements appear or become required based on earlier answers. Tire line details : For some DR Types, tire lines also need Wheel Position, Barcode, OTR Serial Number, or Removed Tire DoT Number. You enter these with the DOT number, and required fields show a red asterisk. Submission : Shows DR Submission , a summary of what will be sent, with any warnings or errors that block it. Select Submit DR when it's clear. Status : Shows TreadNet DR Status , including Current Status, Web DR Number, TreadNet Invoice Number, and Message. Select Fetch Current Status to refresh, or View Invoice once the invoice arrives."}, {"u": "bridgestone-firestone-national-accounts-treadnet.html#after-submission", "t": "After Submission", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts (TreadNet)", "x": "Once the DR is submitted, the order is locked and can only be viewed until TreadNet invoices it. Then you can invoice it in TireWorks HD. Users with the Bridgestone NA - Edit Order Before DR is Invoiced access right can still edit and invoice the order. If TreadNet rejects the DR or needs dealer action, the order becomes editable again so you can correct it and resubmit. The TreadNet invoice PDF is collected automatically after invoicing. Open it from the Status tab, or from the vendor credit for the order during program reconciliation. Tip: Use the Home screen filter to find orders by TreadNet DR Number or Web DR Number. Note: On TreadNet orders, Prod. Code drops leading zeros from tire part numbers to match Bridgestone's invoice format."}, {"u": "bridgestone-firestone-national-accounts-treadnet.html#set-up-dr-sequences", "t": "Set up DR# sequences", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts (TreadNet)", "x": "Go to Manage; Special Programs; Manage Special Programs . Select the TreadNet program, then open the DR# Sequence tab. Enter a DR Number Sequence for each location to number new orders automatically. Leave it blank to type the DR# on each order. Note: Only users with the Bridgestone NA - Override Auto DR Numbers access right can change an automatic DR#."}, {"u": "bridgestone-firestone-national-accounts-treadnet.html#program-reconciliation", "t": "Program reconciliation", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Bridgestone Firestone National Accounts (TreadNet)", "x": "Before you start: You need the Special Programs - Manage Program Reconciliation and Special Programs - View Program Reconciliation Transactions access rights. Manage; Special Programs; Manage Program Reconciliation sets up how a special program's orders are reconciled. You choose whether to add transactions to the reconciliation window, whether to automate the customer credit invoice and vendor credits, the variance threshold (dollar or percent), the vendor, and the credit, misc, commission, and variance SKUs. Link Invoice PDF To AP Invoice attaches the TreadNet PDF to the vendor credit. Assign programs on the Program Association tab. Manage; Special Programs; View Program Reconciliation Transactions lists each order's transactions. Search by Special Program , Reconciliation Status (All, All Incomplete, Open, Submitted, Needs Review, Completed), Dates , and fields such as DR Number, Order Id, or Vendor Invoice Id. Line status : Mark lines Submitted , Review Needed , or Completed , and review Commission, Gain/Loss, and Variance. Create AP Invoice : Creates an AP invoice linked to the order. Requires the Special Programs - Reconcile - New AP Invoice access right."}, {"u": "loyalty-rewards.html", "t": "Loyalty Rewards", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Loyalty Rewards", "x": "Use Loyalty Rewards to see a customer's rewards on a service request, enroll customers, and redeem rewards on the order. This applies when your company uses a loyalty program (Clutch or BayIQ). Your company uses one program at a time."}, {"u": "loyalty-rewards.html#the-rewards-bubble", "t": "The Rewards bubble", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Loyalty Rewards", "x": "The Loyalty Rewards bubble shows at the bottom of the service request once a customer (not the default customer) is on the order. Gift icon : Orange when the customer isn't enrolled, and green when enrolled. Count : How many rewards the customer has available. Applied : The amount of rewards already applied to the order. Select the bubble to open the Loyalty Rewards window. Note: If the reward service can't be reached, the window shows \"WebService Unreachable!\". Select Retry Now ."}, {"u": "loyalty-rewards.html#enroll-a-customer", "t": "Enroll a customer", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Loyalty Rewards", "x": "Before you start: Enrolling a new customer requires the Loyalty Rewards - Enroll Button access right. Updating an enrolled customer doesn't. In the Loyalty Rewards window, select Enroll . The button reads Update once the customer is enrolled. Clutch : If a loyalty customer already exists with the same phone or email, they're listed. Select one and select Done to use it, or select SignUp New to enroll. BayIQ : In the BayiQ Account Selector , search by last name, email, phone, or card number, then select Done or Sign Up . Note: Depending on your company's setup, you may be prompted, or required, to enter the customer's email before enrolling. Tip: Your store can use Order Validation (Reward Program Enrollment) to warn when the customer on an order isn't enrolled."}, {"u": "loyalty-rewards.html#redeem-rewards", "t": "Redeem rewards", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Loyalty Rewards", "x": "Open the Balances tab. It shows Points and the rewards available, with Amount, Description, and Expiry. Select a reward, then select Redeem to apply it to the order. BayIQ rewards with no set value can be redeemed for the amount you enter. Others are limited to their value. Clutch: One reward and one coupon can be applied to an order, unless your company allows multiple cashback rewards. Note: Rewards used on an order are removed from the customer's available list once the order is invoiced. Note: Rewards can't exceed the order total. If they would result in change due to the customer, Order Validation stops the order until the rewards or the order are adjusted."}, {"u": "invoice-reversal-and-copy.html", "t": "Invoice Reversal and Copy", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Invoice Reversal and Copy", "x": "Use Invoice Reversal and Copy to quickly reverse an invoice that's already processed, or to copy an existing invoice to a new order. Before you start: Reverse (Create a Return Order) shows only for closed (invoiced) orders, and needs the Service Request - Reversal access right. Copy (Copy to New Order) shows for orders in any status, and needs the Service Request - Copy Order access right. Open the Service Request search. Enter the search criteria you know."}, {"u": "invoice-reversal-and-copy.html#reverse-an-invoice", "t": "Reverse an invoice", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Invoice Reversal and Copy", "x": "Highlight the invoice. Hover to the left of Request Id and select the reverse function. Confirm that the order should be reversed. Select the reversal date from the calendar, if your access rights allow. Choosing the date needs the Service Request - Change Date on Reversal access right. Without it, the reversal uses today's date. The calendar starts on the original invoice date. Select Done to use the date, or Cancel to stop the reversal. A date whose cash drawer is already reconciled isn't allowed unless you have the Service Request - Set InvoiceDate as CD Reconciled access right. Pick another date. An order can be reversed only once. A reversal (Return Order) can't be reversed or copied. If the order has a card payment, your store may ask whether to refund the card. See Voids, Refunds, and Reversals under Electronic Payments . Review the reversed invoice. It shows as the reverse of the original document. Its status is closed, and it CAN'T be edited. Invoice comments fill in automatically, as shown below. Cost reverses at the cost at the time of the original sale. Order validation still needs to be met before you can save. Print the invoice if needed. Select Save . Select Back to return to the Home screen."}, {"u": "invoice-reversal-and-copy.html#copy-an-invoice", "t": "Copy an invoice", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Invoice Reversal and Copy", "x": "Highlight the invoice. Hover to the left of Request Id and select the copy function. Confirm that the order should be copied. The service request shows an exact copy of the selected invoice, with these differences: The copy uses the current tax percentage for the order's tax schedule, not the rate on the original invoice. A reversal (Return Order) can't be copied. The copy is a new, editable service request. Its status is set by its packages like any new order, not Work Complete. The public comment notes the Request ID it was copied from (\"Order copied from existing Order\"). Add items or make any changes needed. A new Request ID is assigned when the copy is saved. Revise Order isn't needed. Continue with the service request as you would any other."}, {"u": "tire-adjustment.html", "t": "Tire Adjustment", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Tire Adjustment", "x": "Use Tire Adjustment to give a customer credit for an adjusted tire against the sale of the replacement tires. The adjustment details are stored with the service request. Start a new Service Request . Select the customer and vehicle as usual. Add the replacement tires as usual. From the overflow menu, select Tire Adjustments . Select Add More to show a tire position on the Prod. Adj. Detail tab. By default, it shows LF (Left Front). This changes once you select the position. Select the Adjustment Type . Select the Product Code from the ellipsis. The customer's service history shows. Make your selection, then select Done . Enter the DoT Number of the tire being adjusted (up to 15 characters). Enter item comments if needed. Enter the original tread depth. Enter the current tread depth. Percentage Wear is calculated from the tread depth and mileage data you enter. Enter the tire mileage. Select the Removal Reason from the drop-down. Select the Position . Select the Replacement Price Level . Enter the Approval Number . Enter the Replacement Price . Credit Amount is calculated from the Percent Wear field. Select Done . All the information is stored with the service request. Select from either tab. A credit package is added to the service request to offset the sale of the new product."}, {"u": "tire-adjustment.html#return-adjusted-tires-to-the-manufacturer", "t": "Return adjusted tires to the manufacturer", "p": "Section 2: Sales › Tire Adjustment", "x": "Adjusted tires waiting to go back to the manufacturer are listed on the Home screen Purchases tab under Tire Adjustment Credits . Select the items, then select Create Return to start a return purchase order, or Put Away to keep them and remove them from the list. Items clear from the list once their return is processed."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html", "t": "Purchase Order", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Use a purchase order to place a stocking order, or any order that isn't for a service request you already created. Note: To send a purchase order electronically to a vendor, see Vendor Ordering . To enter the vendor's bill or a credit, see AP Invoices and Vendor Credits ."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#create-a-purchase-order", "t": "Create a purchase order", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Go to New; Purchase Order , or select on the Purchases tab of the Home page. Choose the vendor in the Select Vendor window, which opens as soon as the new purchase order opens. To find a vendor, enter search criteria in Look For . If the vendor isn't in the list, check . Highlight the vendor. Select Done . Known vendor information fills in automatically. Enter the Reference . If the same reference number was already used on another purchase order for this vendor, you're warned. With the Inventory Receipt - Allow Duplicate Reference Numbers access right, you can choose to keep it. Without it, enter a different reference number. If the vendor has ordering requirements, the Vendor Requirements window opens. Fill in the values. To reopen it later, select the blue i ( Open Vendor Requirements ) next to Delivery Date . To set a delivery date, select the calendar and choose the month and date. To remove the date, select . Select Add Items . The tire lookup screen ( F1 ) opens automatically, and you can switch to General Search ( F3 ) if needed. If you don't know the SKU, search for the product. For search fields and filters, see Search fields and filters below. If you know the manufacturer SKU, add the item with . Enter the manufacturer item number and quantity, such as 254260,10, and press Enter. The line fills in automatically. Use a comma as the delimiter, with no spaces. Check the box to the left of the item in the search results, or double-click the line. Enter the quantity. Verify the Unit of Measure . Verify or change the cost. The PO cost defaults from the default selected in company setup. Verify the FET, if it applies, and change it if needed. Select Done . Repeat these steps until you've added all items. Select X in the search box to return to the purchase order. Select Save . The next sequential purchase order number is assigned. Select Back to return to the Home screen. The purchase order shows on the Purchases tab with an Open status."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#other-purchase-order-actions", "t": "Other purchase order actions", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Freight : Enter a freight amount in Totals if needed. Requires the Purchase Order - Edit Freight Amount access right. Send PO : For vendors set up for electronic ordering, TireWorks HD checks availability with the vendor first. Each line shows a green check (fully available), a yellow warning (partly available) or a red icon (not available). Select Cancel to go back to the purchase order. Availability shows on each line and costs are updated. Select Continue to send the order. Unavailable lines are removed, partly available lines are reduced to the available quantity, and the vendor's cost is used where the vendor returned one. For vendor setup, see Vendor Ordering . Close : On a partly received purchase order, select Close when the rest isn't coming. Quantities change to match what was received, unreceived items are removed, and the purchase order becomes Fully Received. Close is also on the Purchases tab and in Find; Purchase Order . Requires the Purchase Orders - Close PO access right. For a purchase order linked to a service request, see Additional Features & Functionality under Creating Service Request . Important: Closing a purchase order can't be undone."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#replenish-a-purchase-order", "t": "Replenish a purchase order", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Use Replenish to add items for the selected vendor based on the min/max data set up in inventory management. Select the vendor. Enter the reference information. Select Replenish . Line items fill in based on the min/max data and are flagged as auto generated. Add more line items manually if you want. Select Save when you're done."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#import-items-from-a-spreadsheet", "t": "Import items from a spreadsheet", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Use Import to add items to a purchase order from an Excel spreadsheet. Select Import . Select and choose the file. Select the worksheet from the dropdown. In Sku , select the column header from your spreadsheet. You must use the universal SKU. In Quantity , select the column header from your spreadsheet. In Cost , select the column header from your spreadsheet. A preview displays. After you verify the preview, select ."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#export-a-purchase-order", "t": "Export a purchase order", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Use Export to export the information on the purchase order to an Excel spreadsheet."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#receive-a-purchase-order", "t": "Receive a purchase order", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Use Receive to receive directly from the purchase order. Select Receive . An inventory receipt opens automatically, with the comment \"Created through PO Number:\" and the PO number. Complete the receipt. See Inventory Receipt ."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#search-fields-and-filters", "t": "Search fields and filters", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Global Lookup : Searches by the three-segment universal SKU. Segment 1: Simple tire size, with no dashes, slashes or letters. Segment 2: Manufacturer code, generally the first three characters of the manufacturer. Segment 3: Manufacturer item number. Show Inactive Tires : Search results show all tires, whether active or inactive. Tire Fitment : Defaults to the tire fitment selected for the vehicle. You can choose other fitments. Speed Rating : Defaults based on the tire fitment. Price Level : Defaults to the store default, or to the account default for an A/R customer. Filter : Narrows the search by any part of the description. Advanced Filter : Applies additional filters based on the inventory tree structure. Quantity Available : Total quantity on hand minus committed quantity. Warehouse Quantity : Warehouse quantities, distributor quantities and price, or both. If there are multiple warehouses, you can set it to show only the default servicing warehouse. ASL Quantity : Quantity and price held at all your other stores. Price : The customer's price, set by the store's default price level or the A/R account price level, plus any additional price rules. Tire Detail : Specs, picture, features, comps and warranty information. Available only for tires that are in TDC (Tire Data Central). TDC is a database of over 105,000 tires. Additional Search Filtering : Adds more filters to narrow the search results further. Filtering by Item Group : See the Item Group setup and item assignment procedures."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#vendor-replenishment", "t": "Vendor Replenishment", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Set up vendor replenishment so that Replenish on a purchase order brings in items that need reordering, based on min/max reorder points, the vendor selected, and the submanufacturers defined for that vendor. Note: Each vendor must be mapped to the submanufacturers (brands) it supplies, at each store. Go to Manage; Company Setup; Vendors . Highlight the vendor. You must save a new vendor first. Select Map SubMfrs For Replenish . Vendor SubManufacturer Mapping for Replenishment opens for the store you're logged into. Check each submanufacturer the vendor supplies. Note: Brands under one manufacturer are separate submanufacturers. For Michelin, for example, check Michelin, BFGoodrich and Uniroyal. Select Done . If you have multiple stores, log into each store and repeat these steps, or select Copy SubManufacturers Mapping to copy this store's mapping to other stores. Important: Copying replaces the existing mapping for this vendor at the stores you select. Max Items : Enter the maximum number of items allowed on one purchase order for the vendor, if the vendor has a limit. Leave it blank for no limit."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#schedule-replenishment-purchase-orders", "t": "Schedule replenishment purchase orders", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "Go to Manage; Location Setup; Locations . Select the Auto-Replenishment tab, then the Vendors tab. Select a vendor and add a Replenishment Schedule ."}, {"u": "purchase-order.html#test-replenishment", "t": "Test replenishment", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Purchase Order", "x": "After setup, test replenishment in the application. Open a purchase order for the vendor and select Replenish . Make sure items with reorder points display as expected. Note: Quantities already on open purchase orders are subtracted from the amount added."}, {"u": "vendor-ordering.html", "t": "Vendor Ordering", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Vendor Ordering", "x": "If your store is set up to order electronically from a vendor, TireWorks HD can show the vendor's quantity and price during searches, send purchase orders straight to the vendor, and build replenishment orders on a schedule. Your TCS representative or administrator sets up each connection."}, {"u": "vendor-ordering.html#set-up-a-vendor-for-electronic-ordering", "t": "Set up a vendor for electronic ordering", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Vendor Ordering", "x": "Go to Manage; Company Setup; Vendors . To list only vendors with an online connection, check Show electronic vendors only . Vendor Type : Identifies which ordering system the vendor uses. Types include Michelin BIB, Michelin BWS, TCS Partner, ATD, JW Tires, MaxFinkelstein, Bridgestone Treadnet and OpenWebs. Vendor types beginning with VIP are for VIP-owned inventory. Capabilities : Shows what the connection supports: Qty., Prices, Order and Replenish. Select Refresh Capabilities after a change. Map SubMfrs for Lookup : Controls which brands the vendor is checked for in searches. Map SubMfrs For Replenish is covered under Vendor Replenishment . Max Items : Limits how many items can go on one purchase order to the vendor. Note: Parts suppliers reached through a parts network (for example ISE or IAP sellers, or a direct seller such as O'Reilly) are set up under Manage; Company Setup; Supplier/IAP Seller/Direct Seller and Epicor ISE Configuration ."}, {"u": "vendor-ordering.html#check-vendor-availability-in-searches", "t": "Check vendor availability in searches", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Vendor Ordering", "x": "Order-capable vendors : Show their quantity and price in the F1 Tire Search results, beside your own inventory and your other stores (ASL). Parts suppliers : Show quantity and price on F3 Parts, Parts Resolution, Quick Quote and Appointments."}, {"u": "vendor-ordering.html#send-a-purchase-order-to-the-vendor", "t": "Send a purchase order to the vendor", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Vendor Ordering", "x": "Create the purchase order as usual, then select Send PO . Send PO works only for a vendor that can take orders. If the vendor needs extra details ( Vendor Requirements ), you're asked to fill them in first. TireWorks HD checks availability with the vendor, then shows Availability Results with PO Qty. , PO Cost , Vendor Qty. Avail. and Vendor Cost for each line. Green check: Item available for order. Yellow triangle: Insufficient quantity at supplier, with the quantity available. Red exclamation: Item not found at supplier, or Item found but unavailable. Review the results, then select Continue to send or Cancel to stop. Note: Your administrator chooses the order number your vendor sees on online orders from the Sourcing Manager: the service request number, the purchase order number, or both (SR, PO or PO-SR)."}, {"u": "vendor-ordering.html#automatic-replenishment-orders", "t": "Automatic replenishment orders", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Vendor Ordering", "x": "If your store has a Replenishment Schedule for a vendor (see Vendor Replenishment ), TireWorks HD creates and sends replenishment purchase orders on that schedule, in the store's local time. A replenishment purchase order that can't be sent to the vendor is cancelled automatically, with a comment explaining why. Each run sends an internal text alert to the store for every purchase order or transfer it creates or fails to create. Alerts arrive in the SMS Hub. See Customer Communication (Texting) ."}, {"u": "new-return.html", "t": "New Return", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › New Return", "x": "Use New Return to create a manual return on any product with quantity on hand. New Return automatically creates a return purchase order and a processed inventory receipt that removes the product from inventory. It also creates the AP invoice (vendor credit) unless the System Setting Disable Automatic AP Invoice Generation is on. When that setting is on, create the vendor credit separately. Before you start: Requires the Purchase Orders - New Return access right. Note: When your company uses two-step returns (System Setting Inventory Returns - Two-Step Workflow ), a Return button displays on received purchase orders and processed inventory receipts, so you can start a return from the original document. A processed return inventory receipt shows a Vendor Credit button to create the credit. These buttons need the Two Step Return Process - Return Button and Two Step Return Process - Credit Button access rights. New Return itself works the same either way. See AP Invoices and Vendor Credits ."}, {"u": "new-return.html#open-a-new-return", "t": "Open a new return", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › New Return", "x": "On the Home screen, select , then select New Return ."}, {"u": "new-return.html#add-items-and-process-the-return", "t": "Add items and process the return", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › New Return", "x": "Select the vendor. Enter a Reference , such as an RGA or the supplier's credit invoice number. Select Add Items . Use the standard search to find the product: F1 Tires, F3 All Other, or Quick Add . Double-click the product. Enter the quantity to return as a positive number. Verify or edit the cost. Select Done . Repeat these steps to add more items, if needed. Close the search screen ( X ) to return to New Return. Verify the information is correct. Don't change the quantity to a negative number. Select Process Return . When a dialog box asks you to confirm, select Yes or No . Selecting Yes processes the purchase order and inventory receipt listed in the dialog box, with negative quantities by default. If you use automatic AP invoice generation, the return AP invoice is also created. In the Return PO Success dialog box, which lists the purchase order and inventory receipt numbers, select OK . Print the purchase order, inventory receipt or AP invoice if you want. You return to the Home screen."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html", "t": "Sourcing Manager", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "Use the Sourcing Manager to source product that isn't currently available in your inventory. You can use it directly from the service request, and receive the product there when it arrives. In a service request, shows to the right of a line item when there isn't enough quantity available to complete the service request. Only tires and items marked Inventoried need sourcing. Tires always need sourcing, even when not marked Inventoried. Labor, other charges and fees, shop fees and specifications never need sourcing. Non-catalog engine oil doesn't need sourcing unless your store turns on the System Setting Engine Oil Non-Catalog Requires Sourcing . Tip: If several items need to come from the same supplier, select at the top of the body of the service request. A list of all items on the service request that need sourcing displays. Check the ones to source from the same supplier. All selected lines are added to one sourcing document. Select the sourcing icon to display the sourcing options."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html#quick-adjustment", "t": "Quick Adjustment", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "Use Quick Adjustment to adjust inventory in so you can proceed with the order. This is generally used when you physically have the inventory but the system shows 0 on hand. Select Quick Adjustment . The adjustment screen displays for you to verify. The cost from the service request fills in. The customer comments show that the adjustment was done through the Sourcing Manager, with the name of the customer. The adjustment references the order ID it was done for. Select to process the inventory adjustment. You can print it if necessary. Select Done . You return to the service request, and shows to the right of the line item to indicate the product is now available."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html#sell-negative", "t": "Sell Negative", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "Use Sell Negative to complete the service request, receive payment and generate the invoice before the product is received. This takes your inventory to a negative quantity on hand and uses the product's average cost until the actual product installed on the vehicle is received. Select Sell Negative . When asked to confirm that you want to sell negative, select Yes or No . You return to the service request, and shows to the right of the line item to indicate it's in a status that can now be completed. Note: Because you're selling before the product is received, the average cost may or may not be correct. By default, it uses the average cost from the last time the item was received. Tip: Receiving the product instead of selling negative gives the correct average cost, so the gross profit percentage for the service request is also calculated correctly."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html#outside-purchase", "t": "Outside Purchase", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "Use Outside Purchase to create a purchase order directly from the service request. It shows on the Purchases tab of the Home screen until the purchase order is received. Use it when online ordering isn't available, or when you mostly order from the vendor by phone or fax. Select Outside Purchase . Select the vendor from the dropdown list. Use Look For to narrow the search. If the vendor isn't in the list, check Show All Vendors . Select Done . Enter the Reference Number . We suggest the service request ID. Verify the items to purchase, their cost and quantity. If the cost is different, enter the correct cost. Enter order comments if needed. Select . Select Done . The Outside Purchase icon shows to the right of the line item, telling you the item was ordered as an outside purchase. You can also see it on the Purchases tab of the Home page."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html#receive-an-outside-purchase", "t": "Receive an outside purchase", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "To receive an outside purchase from the service request, select the Outside Purchase icon next to the line item to receive. Tip: To find the customer or service request number, check the reference number field on the Purchases tab. Option 1: Receive from the service request Select the Outside Purchase icon on the line item to receive. If several line items need receiving, select to receive all line items from the supplier. Open the service request. Select . Verify the total to be received. If it's different from the original purchase order, change the quantity in the To Be Received column. Select Done . Select Done again. Important: In the Receive Open Purchase Order and Pending Transfer window, a partly received purchase order shows a Close Purchase Order icon. Select it when the rest isn't coming. Quantities change to match what was received and the purchase order becomes Fully Received. This can't be undone. Note: Closing here requires the Sourcing Manager - Close PO/PO Items Linked to SR and Purchase Orders - Close PO access rights. You return to the service request, and shows to the right of the line item to indicate it's in a status that can now be completed. The sourcing icon stays until all units are received. Note: Receiving or canceling an outside purchase from the Sourcing Manager requires the Sourcing Manager - Receive PO/PO Items Linked to SR or Sourcing Manager - Cancel PO/PO Items Linked to SR access right. Deleting or declining a line with an open purchase order asks what to do with the PO. See Additional Features & Functionality under Creating Service Request . Option 2: Receive from the Purchases tab On the Purchases tab, double-click the purchase order. A message box shows the service request number the purchase order is linked to. Select OK . Select Receive . An inventory receipt is created, referencing the purchase order it was created from. If the quantity received doesn't equal what was ordered on the purchase order, enter the quantity received in the Qty column. Select Process . A printable inventory receipt is created. Quantity on hand and available quantity are updated. The purchase order status is updated to Fully Received or Partially Received. A fully received purchase order is removed from the Purchases tab. A partially received purchase order is marked \"partially received\" in the Status column of the Purchases tab. In the service request, shows to the right of the line item to indicate it's in a status that can now be completed. The sourcing icon stays until all units are received. Tip: Receive the product in the service request or purchase order before you complete the service request. That way the average cost recalculates to the correct cost, and the service request gets the right gross profit percentage."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html#transfer", "t": "Transfer", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "Use Transfer to see product at your other stores and request it with a transfer request. Select Transfer . A grid shows the items that need sourcing, with each item's available quantity at each alternate stocking location. Several items can go on one transfer request. Check the one store to request the items from. All items are checked by default. You can't change the quantity requested on this screen. Enter comments if necessary. Items the store doesn't have enough of are removed from the request, and a message lists them. With the Sourcing - Transfer Request access right, you can keep unavailable items on the request as a backorder instead. Answer No at \"Would you like to remove the unavailable items from this request?\" Select . The transfer request details list the quantity and transfer cost of the product. By default, the cost is priced from the receiving store's price base and price rules. If the System Setting Transfer Pricing Source is set to Sending Location, the sending store's price base and price rules are used. The transfer shows on the Transfers tab of the requesting store's Home page with a status of Requested. It also shows on the Transfers tab of the sending store's Home page with a status of Requested."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html#send-the-transfer-sending-store", "t": "Send the transfer (sending store)", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "Open the transfer from the Transfers tab, pick the product, and verify Qty Sent . The sending transfer document automatically references the requesting store's Order Id in the order comments. Select Send Transfer . When a window asks you to confirm sending the transfer, select Yes or No . A transfer order is created for you to print and send with the product, and the status changes to In Transit on the Transfers tab of both the sending and receiving stores. The receiving store's Transfers tab shows in red to alert them that the product was sent."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html#receive-the-transfer-receiving-store", "t": "Receive the transfer (receiving store)", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "The receiving store receives the product from the Transfers tab or from the service request. Open the transfer from the Transfers tab, or from the service request whose ID is referenced on the transfer documentation, by selecting the transfer icon to the right of the line item. Select . Verify the quantity to receive, or change it if it's different from the quantity on the transfer documentation. If the quantity is different, the transfer invoice to the requesting store is automatically changed to match the amount received. The requesting store is only invoiced through the intercompany account for the product it received. Select Done . Select Done again. Note: When the requesting store receives the product, inventory is relieved from the sending store and added to the requesting store."}, {"u": "sourcing-manager.html#order-online", "t": "Order Online", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Sourcing Manager", "x": "Use Order Online to order online from vendors that take part in electronic ordering. Follow the same steps as for Outside Purchase above. The Order Online window shows an FET column for each item. For Michelin BWS vendors, all offers for the item are shown by fulfiller and delivery. Pick the offer to order. If the online submission fails, the purchase order is canceled. Try again or use Outside Purchase . For the vendors that support online ordering and their setup, see Vendor Ordering . Note: Also use Outside Purchase to order items that will NOT be added to inventory or affect average cost, such as parts from a dealership or junk yard. These generic SKUs are set up under a branch of inventory management as non-inventoried, so they don't update average cost and their QOH is always 0."}, {"u": "unsold-purchases.html", "t": "Unsold Purchases", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Unsold Purchases", "x": "Use Unsold Purchases to create a return or put away items that were bought on a purchase order and haven't been relieved from inventory. Create Return automatically creates a return purchase order and a processed inventory receipt that removes the product from inventory. It also creates the AP invoice (vendor credit) unless the System Setting Disable Automatic AP Invoice Generation is on. Before you start: Requires the Purchase Orders - Unsold Purchases access right. On the Home screen, select , then select Unsold Purchases . Unsold Purchases Items : Lists items with their Receipt ID , Order # and Customer Name . Use Filter to narrow the list by SKU code, vendor, description, order number or customer name. Unsold Cores : Lists cores with quantity available that may need to go back to a supplier. Create Return and Put Away work the same way as below. See Parts Cores ."}, {"u": "unsold-purchases.html#create-a-return", "t": "Create a return", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Unsold Purchases", "x": "Select the items to return. Selecting several items for the same vendor produces one transaction with multiple items. Select Create Return . Verify the information is correct. Don't change the quantity to a negative number. Select Process Return . When a dialog box asks you to confirm, select Yes or No . Selecting Yes processes the purchase order and inventory receipt listed in the dialog box, with negative quantities by default. If you use automatic AP invoice generation, the return AP invoice is also created. In the Return PO Success dialog box, which lists the purchase order and inventory receipt numbers, select OK . Print the purchase order, inventory receipt or AP invoice if you want. You return to the Home screen."}, {"u": "unsold-purchases.html#put-items-away", "t": "Put items away", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Unsold Purchases", "x": "Select the items to put away. Putting an item away keeps it and removes it from the list. Selecting several items for the same vendor produces one transaction with multiple items. Select Put Away . When a warning asks you to confirm removing the items from the list, select Yes or No . You return to the Home screen."}, {"u": "inventory-receipt.html", "t": "Inventory Receipt", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Inventory Receipt", "x": "Use an inventory receipt to receive product from a vendor into inventory."}, {"u": "inventory-receipt.html#create-an-inventory-receipt", "t": "Create an inventory receipt", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Inventory Receipt", "x": "Go to New; Inventory Receipt . Choose the vendor in the Select Vendor window, which opens as soon as the new inventory receipt opens. Begin typing in Look For to narrow the search. Vendor information fills in from the vendor record. Enter a Reference . This field is required. A reference number already used on another inventory receipt for this vendor gives a warning. With the Inventory Receipt - Allow Duplicate Reference Numbers access right, you can choose to keep it. Without it, enter a different reference number. To use a date other than today, select the calendar next to Received . Requires the Inventory Receipt - Change Received Date access right. Verify the cost to use. The default cost is set in Manage; Company Setup; Company , on the Default Costs tab, which can set a different default cost for each document type and SkuType. To use a different cost, check Use Other Cost and select a cost from the dropdown. Add items using one of these four methods: Add Items : Enter items through the tire search screen. Quick Add : Enter items here if you know the item number. Separate the SKU, quantity and cost with a comma or plus sign . The whole line fills in at once, and you return to Quick Add, ready to add the next item. Receive from multiple PO's : Receive items from more than one purchase order. Choose items from multiple PO's : Enter an item number to see the POs the item is open on. Select the vendor, enter the manufacturer item number in the filter, then enter the quantity to receive and press Enter. Note: Receipt lines show PO Qty , PO Outstanding , Qty Received and Qty Expected . Qty Expected can't be more than PO Outstanding (or PO Qty ) or less than Qty Received , and can't be 0. Qty Received can't be more than Qty Expected . If your store turns on the System Setting Inventory Receipt - Populate Quantity Received , Qty Received fills in with the outstanding quantity. Otherwise it starts at 0. The item drops into the shopping cart, and the cursor returns to the filter field for the next item. When all items are in the cart, select . All items are added to the receipt. Add all items from a PO : Select one complete purchase order. Select the vendor, enter the PO number, and enter the quantity to receive for each line item. When all items are in the cart, select . All items are added to the receipt. Import : Import items from a spreadsheet. A dialog box opens for you to fill in. Select the ellipsis ( ... ) and choose the spreadsheet file to load. Select the worksheet to use from the Worksheet dropdown. Select the Sku column header to use from the preview. Select the quantity column header, typically the count column. Select the cost column, typically the average cost column. Set Original Qty. Source to on hand or file. If you select File , choose the column to use, typically the QOH column. Select Import . The items fill in on the inventory receipt. Verify the total adjustment quantity in TWHD matches the total quantity in the loading document. Select Save to assign a receipt number. You don't need to save if you're processing right away. The receipt saves automatically when you select Process . Select Process . A dialog box confirms the receipt processed successfully. If the receipt has items from more than one purchase order, Choose Process Type asks what to do with unreceived items: Process as is , Cancel unreceived items from the original PO , or Move unreceived items to new PO . Then select Continue Processing . Items with $0 cost ask you to confirm before processing. Select Print if you want. Note: Inventory receipts can be created for items that are NOT marked inventoried in inventory maintenance. To stop non-inventoried items from being received, uncheck the access right in Manage; Access Rights . Note: When your company uses two-step returns, processed receipts show Return and Vendor Credit buttons. See New Return and AP Invoices and Vendor Credits ."}, {"u": "ap-invoices-and-vendor-credits.html", "t": "AP Invoices and Vendor Credits", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › AP Invoices and Vendor Credits", "x": "An AP invoice records what your store owes a vendor for product received. A vendor credit is an AP invoice for a return, recording what the vendor owes you back. Both open in the same AP Invoice window."}, {"u": "ap-invoices-and-vendor-credits.html#when-ap-invoices-are-created", "t": "When AP invoices are created", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › AP Invoices and Vendor Credits", "x": "By default, TireWorks HD creates the AP invoice for you when an inventory receipt is processed, and the vendor credit when a return is processed. If your company turns on the System Setting Disable Automatic AP Invoice Generation , no AP invoice or vendor credit is created automatically. Create them yourself with New; AP Invoice or the Vendor Credit button. See Two-Step Returns below."}, {"u": "ap-invoices-and-vendor-credits.html#create-an-ap-invoice", "t": "Create an AP invoice", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › AP Invoices and Vendor Credits", "x": "Go to New; AP Invoice . In the vendor selection window, which opens right away, search with Look For , highlight the vendor, and select Done . You can create an AP invoice for any vendor, not only preferred vendors. Enter the vendor's invoice number in Reference . A Reference is required before the invoice can be processed. You're alerted if the same reference number was already used for this vendor. Add lines: Receipt Items : Opens Add Inventory Receipt Items . Filter by PO # or Item # , check the received items to bill, and add them. Receipt Cost and Variance show how the invoice cost compares to what was received. Add Items : Search for and add items directly. Verify the Payment terms, Tax Rate and Discount % . Enter Freight if the vendor charged it. Freight entered on the purchase order carries to the receipt and the AP invoice. Editing Freight requires the AP Invoice - Edit Freight Amount access right. Select Save to keep working later, or Process to finalize. Important: A processed AP invoice can no longer be edited."}, {"u": "ap-invoices-and-vendor-credits.html#other-ap-invoice-actions", "t": "Other AP invoice actions", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › AP Invoices and Vendor Credits", "x": "Payment : Records a payment against the invoice. Enter the Payment Type , Payment Amount and Comments , then select Apply and Done . Cancel : Cancels the AP invoice after you confirm."}, {"u": "ap-invoices-and-vendor-credits.html#find-an-ap-invoice", "t": "Find an AP invoice", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › AP Invoices and Vendor Credits", "x": "Go to Find; AP Invoice . Search by Invoice Id , Vendor (or All), Dates and Status (All, Open, Processed, Cancelled). Results show the Reference No. , Create Date , Invoiced Date and Accounting Integration status. Open or print from the result line."}, {"u": "ap-invoices-and-vendor-credits.html#two-step-returns", "t": "Two-Step Returns", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › AP Invoices and Vendor Credits", "x": "If your company uses two-step returns, you can start a return from the original purchase order or receipt, then create the vendor credit as a separate step. Return : Displays on fully or partially received purchase orders (the Purchase Order window, Find; Purchase Order , and the Home screen Purchases tab) and on processed inventory receipts (the Inventory Receipt window and Find; Inventory Receipt ). Return on a purchase order creates a return purchase order. Return on a receipt creates a return inventory receipt and opens it for review. A document can only be returned once, and a return can't itself be returned. Vendor Credit : Displays on the return inventory receipt once it's processed. Select it and confirm to create the vendor credit, which opens in the AP Invoice window. Note: These buttons require the Two Step Return Process - Return Button and Two Step Return Process - Credit Button access rights. Note: The Inventory Returns - Two-Step Workflow setting only adds the Return and Vendor Credit buttons. It doesn't change New Return or Unsold Purchases Create Return , which still create and process the return purchase order and return inventory receipt in one step. Whether the vendor credit is created automatically depends only on Disable Automatic AP Invoice Generation ."}, {"u": "ap-invoices-and-vendor-credits.html#link-bridgestone-treadnet-invoices", "t": "Link Bridgestone (TreadNet) invoices", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › AP Invoices and Vendor Credits", "x": "If your store orders from a Bridgestone TreadNet vendor, a Link Bridgestone Invoice button displays on that vendor's AP invoices. Select Link Bridgestone Invoice . Unlinked Bridgestone Invoices opens, listing Invoice Date , Invoice No. and Invoice Total . Select View to preview the PDF. Select Link Invoice . Once an invoice PDF is linked, View National Account Invoice opens it."}, {"u": "inventory-adjustment.html", "t": "Inventory Adjustment", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Inventory Adjustment", "x": "Use an inventory adjustment to adjust inventory for items you add from a search, enter with Quick Add, or import from a spreadsheet."}, {"u": "inventory-adjustment.html#create-an-inventory-adjustment", "t": "Create an inventory adjustment", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Inventory Adjustment", "x": "Go to New; Inventory Adjustment . Enter the reference information. This field is required. Enter any User Comments . Total Units keeps a running total as you enter items. Add the items to adjust, using the method that fits the task: Add Items : Enter items through the tire search screen. Quick Add : Enter items here if you know the item number. Separate the SKU, quantity and cost with commas . The whole line fills in at once, and you return to Quick Add, ready to add the next item. Import : Import items from a spreadsheet. A dialog box opens for you to fill in. Select the ellipsis ( ... ) and choose the spreadsheet file to load. Select the worksheet to use from the Worksheet dropdown. Select the Sku column header to use from the preview. Select the quantity column header, typically the count column. Select the cost column, typically the average cost column. Set Original Qty. Source to on hand or file. If you select File , choose the column to use, typically the QOH column. Select Import . The items fill in on the inventory adjustment. Verify the total adjustment quantity in TWHD matches the total quantity in the loading document. Select Save to assign an Adjustment ID. Select Process . A dialog box confirms the adjustment processed successfully. Select Print if you want."}, {"u": "inventory-adjustment.html#delete-or-comment-on-a-line", "t": "Delete or comment on a line", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Inventory Adjustment", "x": "Delete a line : Hover to the left of the item number and select the minus sign. Add a line comment : Hover to the left of the item number and select the comment icon."}, {"u": "inventory-adjustment.html#import-costs", "t": "Import Costs", "p": "Section 3: Purchasing & Receiving › Inventory Adjustment", "x": "Use Import Costs to update costs, quantities, reorder points and price bases for existing items from an Excel spreadsheet. It doesn't create new items. Before you start: Requires the Inventory - Import Costs access right. Go to Manage; Utilities; Import Costs . In Excel File , select ... and choose the file, then pick the WorkSheet . In Map on , choose Manufacturer Sku or Universal Sku , then pick the Location(s) and Sub Manufacturer . Under Map Inventory Columns , pick the spreadsheet column for each value to update, for example Invoice , Average , Last , FET , Qnty On Hand , Min ReOrder Qnty and Max ReOrder Qnty . Under Map Price Bases , pick columns for any price bases to update. Select LookUp Items to see how many items match, then select Import . Confirm the matching item count and the prompt that the import is long running. A message shows how many items were updated."}, {"u": "transfers.html", "t": "Transfers", "p": "Section 4: Transfers › Transfers", "x": "Use a transfer to move product between locations. You can also create a transfer from within a service request. To start, go to New; Transfer ."}, {"u": "transfers.html#create-a-transfer-request", "t": "Create a transfer request", "p": "Section 4: Transfers › Transfers", "x": "Select the Transfer Direction . Select Send items if you will be sending product. Select Receive items if you will be receiving product. Search for product. Press F1 for tires or F3 for all other inventoried product. The search results show the WHSE quantity and ASL quantity. WHSE Quantity : quantity in the distribution warehouse. ASL Quantity : quantity in all locations, including warehouse locations. You can set which locations can be viewed, by location. A checkbox lets you view all locations when checked. Choose the product you want, and then select . Enter the quantity you want, and verify that all other needed information is filled in. Requesting more than the sending location has available needs the Transfer - Transfer Request access right. Close the search screen. Select the sending location from the dropdown. Enter Comments if needed. Select Save . The transfer ID and header information display. Select Send Request . In the confirmation dialog box, select Yes to continue, or No to go back to the transfer. The printable transfer order displays. Select to return to the Home screen."}, {"u": "transfers.html#after-you-send-a-request", "t": "After you send a request", "p": "Section 4: Transfers › Transfers", "x": "The transfer request displays on the requesting store's Transfers tab. Retail sending location : the request also displays on the sending store's Transfers tab. Wholesale sending location : the request automatically fills in a sales order at the Wholesale location. While a Wholesale user has the transfer open, Retail shows \"The linked transfer is currently locked. You cannot access this transfer.\" Try again later. The transfer shows In Transit on the Retail side until your store receives it. Your store can cancel a request sent to a Wholesale warehouse by selecting Cancel on the transfer. This needs the Cancel Transfer Request access right."}, {"u": "transfers.html#send-a-transfer", "t": "Send a transfer", "p": "Section 4: Transfers › Transfers", "x": "When the sending location is a Retail store, the sending store opens the transfer from the Transfers tab on the Home screen. Verify or fill in the sent quantity. Sending more than was requested needs the Transfer - Increase Sending Quantity access right. Without it, you see \"You do not have the access rights to send more than requested\" and the quantity is set back to the requested amount. Transfer cost fills in automatically, priced as set by the Transfer Pricing Source setting (receiving location by default). Select Send Transfer . In the confirmation dialog box, select Yes to continue, or No to go back to the transfer. The transfer saves automatically, and the Transfer Order displays for printing. The transfer now shows a status of In Transit on the sending store's Transfers tab. The product is allocated in the sending store's inventory. Inventory is not relieved until the receiving location has received the product. The transfer order shows the Linked Transfer ID , which is the transfer ID of the requesting location. Deliver a copy of the transfer order with the product. Note: You can change Order Comments at any point in the transfer. Select Save under Order Comments to keep the change."}, {"u": "transfers.html#receive-a-transfer", "t": "Receive a transfer", "p": "Section 4: Transfers › Transfers", "x": "The Transfers tab at the receiving location lights up red when a transfer needs action. Double-click the transfer. Linked Transfer ID shows the transfer ID of the sending location. Verify that the quantity is correct. If it is not, enter the correct received amount. Select Receive Transfer . A dialog box confirms the transfer has been received. Select to return to the Home screen. The transfer disappears from the Home screen Transfers tab because it is complete. Note: Inventory is relieved at the sending location and increases at the receiving location when you receive the transfer. A transfer can be received only once. Note: If less is received than was sent, an email goes to the address in the System Setting Transfer Recipient Email , when your store has one set. Important: Always receive inventory before you add it to a sales order, so the average cost is accurate. Tip: Create the transfer from within the service request, so you don't have to leave the service request. The service request ID displays in the comments of the sending location's paperwork, which makes receiving easier. The correct cost is assigned as long as the product is received before invoicing. See Sourcing Manager ."}, {"u": "inventory-replenishment.html", "t": "Inventory replenishment", "p": "Section 4: Transfers › Inventory replenishment", "x": "Inventory replenishment creates a transfer request from the Min/Max data in the inventory master file. It can be set up for manual or automatic replenishment. The steps below cover manual replenishment."}, {"u": "inventory-replenishment.html#replenish-inventory-manually", "t": "Replenish inventory manually", "p": "Section 4: Transfers › Inventory replenishment", "x": "Go to New; Transfer . Select Receive items . Select the distribution warehouse that is replenishing the product. Select . Product fills in based on the Min/Max data and availability at the distribution warehouse. Add, remove or change quantities as needed. Note: The suggested quantity is the Max reorder point minus the quantity on hand and minus the quantity already on order. By default, committed quantity is also subtracted from on hand. If your store sets the System Setting Reorder Point Calculation Method to QoH, committed quantity is not subtracted. Select Save when you are done. Select . A prompt asks you to confirm sending the transfer request. The transfer request displays for printing. The request shows on the Home screen Transfers tab, with a status of Requested, at both the requesting and sending location until the request is filled. Note: For automatic replenishment setup, see Locations Setup and Maintenance , Auto-Replenishment tab."}, {"u": "cash-drawer.html", "t": "Cash Drawer", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Cash Drawer", "x": "Use Cash Drawer to manage petty cash and reconcile the cash drawer. It also gives you an at-a-glance look at sales at any time of day, both in dollars and in number of transactions. To open it, select Cash Drawer on the application toolbar."}, {"u": "cash-drawer.html#configure-cash-drawer-settings", "t": "Configure cash drawer settings", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Cash Drawer", "x": "Select Configure . Configure has three tabs: Company Txn. Types , Location Txn. Types and Misc. Settings . On the Misc. Settings tab, under Configure Misc. Location Settings , enter a cash value in Default Remaining Cash . Select Save . A message confirms the changes were saved."}, {"u": "cash-drawer.html#set-up-transaction-types-and-gl-accounts", "t": "Set up transaction types and GL accounts", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Cash Drawer", "x": "Company Txn. Types : add petty cash transaction types ( Txn. Type Code , Description , Expense Account , Default Direction , Upper Limit , Print Receipt Required ), and then select Save . Location Txn. Types : pick a location, set each transaction type's Default Printer , Print Receipt and Active , and then select Save . Misc. Settings : under Configure Misc. Company Settings , pick the GL Account for each credit card and other item. Select None to clear a GL Account."}, {"u": "cash-drawer.html#record-a-petty-cash-transaction", "t": "Record a petty cash transaction", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Cash Drawer", "x": "Select the transaction type from the dropdown list. Enter the Amount of the transaction. Verify the default Direction , or change it from the dropdown if needed. Enter the Transaction Description . Verify or select the Print Receipt box. Select Save . To remove the transaction data instead, select Clear . The items display on the Transaction List . You can filter the list by the dropdown date ranges or a custom date range. You can print the list."}, {"u": "cash-drawer.html#reconcile-daily-transactions", "t": "Reconcile daily transactions", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Cash Drawer", "x": "Verify the Deposit date . Select the dropdown box to view a calendar. The reconciliation window has these sections: Sales : shows daily sales by payment method. Credit Card Detail displays above the credit card sales totals. Total sales : the sum of all payment types, which is the total sales for the selected deposit date. Counts : shows the number of transactions by transaction type, by default. Select to view the totals in dollars. Invoices then equal total sales. Cash Drawer : used to reconcile cash and prepare the bank deposit. Beginning Cash on Hand : the daily beginning balance. Cash In : equals the amount in Cash Sales. Check Receipts : equals the amount in Check Sales. Total Cash/Check In : beginning cash on hand plus cash in and check receipts. ROAs : total ROA payments collected. Misc Income : petty cash \"In\" transactions. Customer Deposits (Total Collected) : total customer deposits collected by cash, check and credit card. Paid Outs : petty cash \"Out\" transactions. Vendor Payments : vendor payments from AP invoices for the day. BANK DEPOSIT : the only editable field. Enter the total amount of the bank deposit, which includes customer deposits, ROAs, and petty cash in or out. Ending Cash on Hand : starts at the Default Remaining Cash set in the cash drawer configuration. It drops below that amount only when paid outs and vendor payments are more than the cash taken in, and it is $0 when Total Cash/Check Out is more than Total Cash/Check In. Any other difference goes to Over/Short. When the System Setting CD - Keep Cash on Hand at Fixed Value is on, entering the bank deposit does not change Ending Cash on Hand. Over/Short : Total Cash/Check Out (paid outs, vendor payments and bank deposit) plus Ending Cash on Hand, minus Total Cash/Check In. A positive amount is over, and a negative amount is short. Enter the BANK DEPOSIT amount. To add a comment, select , enter your text, and close the comment dialog box. The comment saves with the daily cash drawer. Credit Card details Select Reconcile when the cash drawer reconciliation is complete. A message tells you the reconciliation is complete, and a green check mark shows that the daily transactions are saved and reconciled. Select Print to print the report for store or corporate office records. Tip: Print the payout transactions for the day and attach them to the cash drawer report. Select Commit after you review the reconciliation. A confirmation window warns that the action can't be undone and asks whether to continue. Select No to go back to the reconciled cash drawer. Select Yes to commit. A message confirms the reconciliation was committed successfully. Important: Committing a reconciliation can't be undone."}, {"u": "cash-drawer.html#reports-that-help-with-reconciliation", "t": "Reports that help with reconciliation", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Cash Drawer", "x": "Sales Tender : recommended. Payment Type Totals : use when you are looking for credit card detail. Summary of Invoices Note: These reports run from your store's report server. Report names and folders can differ. If you can't find one, ask your administrator."}, {"u": "payroll-entry.html", "t": "Payroll Entry", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Payroll Entry", "x": "Use Payroll Entry to record each technician's and salesperson's hours for the week, by store, and to print a Weekly Payroll report. Before you start: You need the Payroll Entry access right. Without it, Payroll Entry is grayed out on the New menu."}, {"u": "payroll-entry.html#enter-weekly-hours", "t": "Enter weekly hours", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Payroll Entry", "x": "Go to New; Payroll Entry . Weekly Payroll opens on the current week for your store. To work on another store you have access to, choose it in Location . Week Ending shows the Sunday that ends the week. Weeks run Monday through Sunday. Week shows the week number of the year. To open a different week, select ... beside Week Ending and pick any date in that week. Select Add Employee . Choose Technician or Salesperson , and then select ... to pick the person. For a salesperson, use Look For to filter and Show In-Active User to include inactive users, and then select Done . An employee can be added only once per week. Enter Work hours, Vacation hours, Holiday hours, Sick hours, Personal hours, Bereavement hours, Jury Duty hours and Salary hours. Total hours adds them up. If the employee has been terminated, check Terminate . Select Done . Select Save . \"Weekly Payroll saved successfully!\" displays. A week with no employees can't be saved. Select Print to save and print the Weekly Payroll report. Select Back to leave. If there are unsaved changes, you are asked to save them first. Select Yes to save or No to discard. The same question displays if you change Location with unsaved changes."}, {"u": "payroll-entry.html#change-or-remove-an-entry", "t": "Change or remove an entry", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Payroll Entry", "x": "Change an entry : double-click the employee's line. Remove an entry : select the delete icon on the line and answer Yes to \"Are you sure you want to delete this Payroll item?\" Note: Each store's week is saved separately. Pick the store in Location before entering hours."}, {"u": "customer-deposits.html", "t": "Customer deposits", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer deposits", "x": "Use a customer deposit to take one or more deposits on an existing service request. The deposit shows in the Add Payment section of the service request, so you can apply it when you invoice. To start, go to New; Customer Deposit ."}, {"u": "customer-deposits.html#add-a-deposit", "t": "Add a deposit", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer deposits", "x": "At Select Customer , enter the customer lookup information. Select the customer. To use a different customer, search again. You can change the customer only before the deposit is saved. Select to the right of Order Id , and select the order to apply the deposit to. Enter a description. It is required and limited to 150 characters. Enter the payment information. Enter a positive amount. Negative amounts are not accepted. Customer Deposit is not a payment type on an ROA. After each payment is applied, Payment Type goes back to Cash and the amount clears. Pick the payment type again for the next payment. Each payment type asks for its own information. For card payments, see Electronic Payments . If a card payment fails and you don't enter it manually, you can try again. If you close or cancel with no payment taken, the deposit is marked Canceled and a note is added to its description. Select . The payment displays under Added Payments . Select Save . Select Print to print the customer deposit receipt. The deposit displays in the Add Payments section of the service request. Note: You can take multiple deposits or installments, either under one deposit or as multiple deposits."}, {"u": "customer-deposits.html#refund-a-deposit", "t": "Refund a deposit", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer deposits", "x": "Before you start: Your company must allow deposit refunds. On a saved deposit, select Refund . On a partly applied deposit, the button is Refund Unused Amount . Confirm the refund. Add the refund payments. Select Save ."}, {"u": "customer-deposits.html#reprint-or-find-a-customer-deposit", "t": "Reprint or find a customer deposit", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer deposits", "x": "Go to Find; Customer Deposit . Enter the search criteria you know, and then select Search . To the left of Deposit Id , select the option to print or open the customer deposit."}, {"u": "customer-deposits.html#reverse-a-customer-deposit", "t": "Reverse a customer deposit", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer deposits", "x": "Search for the deposit with the information you have. Select the deposit to reverse. Hover to the left of Deposit Id and select Open Customer Deposit . Select Reverse . Enter a Reason for Reversal . It is required. Select Process Reversal . A new Deposit Id is created, and its description references the original Deposit Id. Note: Only a deposit in Received status can be reversed. A reversed deposit or a reversal can't be reversed again. If the deposit was paid by a check processed electronically, you are asked how to handle the check. Select Yes to reverse without an electronic check reversal, No to change the check payment to Cash so you can refund from the drawer, or Cancel to stop. Card payments are voided or refunded. See Electronic Payments . If your store sets the System Setting CD with Electronic Payment Reversal not to reverse electronically, void or refund the card outside TireWorks HD. If you select print, the original Deposit Id prints with the reversal information."}, {"u": "customer-deposits.html#print-a-reversal", "t": "Print a reversal", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer deposits", "x": "Go to Find; Customer Deposit . Enter the search criteria. The reversal displays with a status of Reversal . The original deposit displays with a status of Reversed . Hover to the left of the reversal and select Print . Note: You can delete a payment from a customer deposit by selecting before you save the deposit. After the deposit is saved, you must reverse it instead."}, {"u": "customer-roa-payments.html", "t": "Customer ROA payments", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer ROA payments", "x": "Use Customer ROA to take a payment on account, produce a receipt, and apply the payment directly to the customer's account."}, {"u": "customer-roa-payments.html#take-an-roa-payment", "t": "Take an ROA payment", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer ROA payments", "x": "Go to New; Customer ROA . Enter the Company Name and select the customer from the list. The customer's open invoices display. Displays the payment history. Takes you back to the first search. Choose how to apply the payment. applies it to the oldest invoices first, until the total payment has been used. Lets you apply the payment invoice by invoice. Select the invoices to pay, to the left of the document number. Select Payment Total . Enter the payment information. Select Apply . The applied payments display. Select Done . The payment amount displays by document number. Select Process Payments . The receipt displays, with a customer copy and a store copy. ROA payments appear in the cash drawer for the day the payment was received. Close the Receipt on Account screen."}, {"u": "customer-roa-payments.html#reprint-or-find-an-roa-payment", "t": "Reprint or find an ROA payment", "p": "Section 5: Daily Cash Balancing & Other Payment Collection › Customer ROA payments", "x": "Go to Find; ROA . Enter the search criteria you know, and then select Search . Hover to the left of the ROA ID you want, and select the icon to open the ROA. On the Receipt on Account screen, select . Hover to the left of ROA Id and select the printer icon to reprint the ROA. Print the ROA if needed. Select Done in the Payment History window. Close the Receipt on Account screen."}, {"u": "access-group-setup-and-access-rights-assignment.html", "t": "Access Group Setup and Access Rights Assignment", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Access Group Setup and Access Rights Assignment", "x": "Use access groups to give users with similar job duties and responsibilities the same access rights. To open this screen, go to Manage; Company Setup; Access Rights ."}, {"u": "access-group-setup-and-access-rights-assignment.html#create-an-access-group", "t": "Create an access group", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Access Group Setup and Access Rights Assignment", "x": "Select the Copy Security Profile tab. In the Profile List , highlight the security profile to copy from. Enter the new group name in New Profile Name , then select Copy Profile . The message \"'[profile]' profile has been successfully copied as '[new name]'.\" displays. Select OK . Select Save ."}, {"u": "access-group-setup-and-access-rights-assignment.html#set-a-group-s-view-and-edit-rights", "t": "Set a group's view and edit rights", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Access Group Setup and Access Rights Assignment", "x": "Select the General tab. Check the boxes for the view and edit capabilities the group needs in each module. Select Save ."}, {"u": "access-group-setup-and-access-rights-assignment.html#set-a-group-s-search-result-fields", "t": "Set a group's search result fields", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Access Group Setup and Access Rights Assignment", "x": "The Search Results tab sets the same search result fields for every member of the access group. Note: You can also manage search result fields at the user level. On the Search Results tab, select a Search Type from the dropdown. Highlight the field you want in Available Fields . Select to move it to Assigned Fields . To move all fields to Assigned Fields , select . To remove a field from Assigned Fields , highlight it and select . To remove all fields from Assigned Fields , select ."}, {"u": "access-group-setup-and-access-rights-assignment.html#after-you-save-access-rights", "t": "After you save access rights", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Access Group Setup and Access Rights Assignment", "x": "When you save, TireWorks HD asks \"Would you like to refresh your user session for these changes to take effect?\" Select Yes . Other users see the change after Help; Refresh User Session or logging out and back in. Note: VIEW and EDIT boxes only show where they have an effect for that access right. Note: Each window under Manage has its own access right. A user sees only the Manage menu items their profile has View for. The Manage menu itself shows only when the profile has View on \"Manage All\"."}, {"u": "comment-setup-maintenance.html", "t": "Comment Setup & Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Comment Setup & Maintenance", "x": "Use comment setup to create the comments your stores use often, group them, and assign them by store. To open this screen, go to Manage; Company Setup; Comments ."}, {"u": "comment-setup-maintenance.html#add-a-comment", "t": "Add a comment", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Comment Setup & Maintenance", "x": "Select the Comments tab. Select Add . In Comment Code , enter the comment abbreviation. In Comment , enter the comment description that appears on the service request. Select the Specification Type/Service Type . Make sure Active is checked. Select Save ."}, {"u": "comment-setup-maintenance.html#inactivate-a-comment", "t": "Inactivate a comment", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Comment Setup & Maintenance", "x": "Comments can't be deleted, only inactivated. Highlight the comment and clear the Active box. Select Save ."}, {"u": "comment-setup-maintenance.html#edit-a-comment", "t": "Edit a comment", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Comment Setup & Maintenance", "x": "Highlight the comment and edit the information. Select Save . Note: By default, only active comments display in the comment list. Select to view all comments."}, {"u": "comment-setup-maintenance.html#add-a-comment-group", "t": "Add a comment group", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Comment Setup & Maintenance", "x": "Select the Comment Groupings tab. Select Add . In Comment Group Code , enter the group name. Enter the Comment Group Description . Select and select a comment from the list. Repeat until you have added all the comments. Select Save ."}, {"u": "comment-setup-maintenance.html#edit-a-comment-group", "t": "Edit a comment group", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Comment Setup & Maintenance", "x": "Note: You can't inactivate a comment group today. Instead, we suggest changing its Comment Group Code to DO NOT USE. Highlight the comment group and edit the information. Select Save ."}, {"u": "comment-setup-maintenance.html#remove-a-comment-from-a-group", "t": "Remove a comment from a group", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Comment Setup & Maintenance", "x": "In the Comments list, highlight the comment to delete. Select Delete . Select Save ."}, {"u": "tax-details.html", "t": "Tax details", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Tax details", "x": "Use Tax Detail to set up the tax details, such as rates and types, that your tax schedules use. Go to Manage; Company Setup; Tax Detail . Select Add . Enter the Tax Detail Id , Description , Tax Detail Type and Tax Detail Percent . Enter the Account Number , Tax Detail Amount , Account Segment and Taxable Tax as needed. Enterprise Zone : Check if the tax detail is an enterprise zone rate. The Sku Type Tax Rate tab then opens so you can set a Tax Detail Percent for each SKU Type. If your company uses QuickBooks Online, pick a Tax Agency before saving. See QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager . Select Save . At the warning \"Once saved, the Tax Detail Id, Type and Percent cannot be changed\", select Yes . Important: Fields marked with * can't be edited once they are saved. Check them before saving."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html", "t": "Locations Setup and Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Use Locations to maintain each store's information and settings. Each tab below covers one area of store setup. To open this screen, go to Manage; Location Setup; Locations ."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#general-tab", "t": "General tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "TCS sets up new stores during implementation. You can fill in additional information as needed. Highlight the store. Enter additional information as needed. Select Save . Note: You can use the store license number field to hold any extra store information that has no field of its own, such as a NonSig number. Signature Capture : Check to have this store ask customers to approve orders. See Customer Approval ."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#tax-tab", "t": "Tax tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Highlight the store. Select the tax schedule from the dropdown. Check Use Location Tax if tax is based on the store where the service work was performed. Select Save ."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#orderstate-labels-tab", "t": "OrderState Labels tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Give the default order statuses your own labels to match your company's practice. Highlight the store. Select and highlight the status to change. Click in the customer label column and enter the label. Select Save ."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#search-defaults-tab", "t": "Search Defaults tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Set search defaults by store and search type. You can also set search defaults for a single user. Highlight the store. Select the search type. Use the right arrow to move columns from Available Columns to Selected Columns . Hold CTRL to select several columns. Hold SHIFT to select a range of columns. To remove a column, use the left arrow to move it out of Selected Columns . Use the up and down arrows to set the order the columns display in. Select Save ."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#preferred-vendors-tab", "t": "Preferred Vendors tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Limit the vendor dropdown on purchase orders and outside purchases to the vendors for this store. A checkbox in the application lets you select all vendors if needed. Highlight the store. Select vendors in the Available Vendors list. Select Add to move them from Available Vendors to Preferred Vendors . Hold CTRL to select several vendors. Hold SHIFT to select a range of vendors. To remove a vendor from Preferred Vendors , select Remove . Use the up and down arrows to arrange the vendors. By default, vendors are in alphabetical order by vendor ID. Select Save . Note: You don't need to log into each store to do this."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#remove-preferred-vendors", "t": "Remove preferred vendors", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Select the store. Select the Preferred Vendors tab. In the Preferred Vendors list, highlight the vendors to remove. The list displays alphabetically. To select a range, select the first vendor, hold SHIFT and select the second vendor. All vendors between them are highlighted. To select several specific vendors, select one vendor, then hold CTRL and select each additional vendor. Select Remove . Select Save when you're done."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#auto-replenishment-tab", "t": "Auto-Replenishment tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Auto-Replenishment automatically creates a transfer request from min/max data and submits it to the Primary Distribution Location. Highlight the store. Select the TireWorks® HD Wholesale tab and check Auto-Replenishment . Select the Primary Distribution Location from the dropdown. Select the days of the week to replenish. Consider the fulfillment location's hours of operation when you set the days and times. Select to the right of the time column. The time field displays only when the day of the week is checked. Enter the time in military time. Select Save . Note: The transfer request is generated and submitted automatically. The transfer order is created in the sending location. Order Only What Can Be Fulfilled : Check to request only items the Primary Distribution Location has available. Sku Types : Check the SKU types to replenish. Only items of the checked SKU types are requested. Copy SkuTypes : Copies this store's SKU types to other stores. Vendors tab : Sets up scheduled replenishment purchase orders from vendors. See Vendor Replenishment ."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#other-locations-tabs", "t": "Other Locations tabs", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "These tabs are normally set up with TCS during implementation. Accounting : accounting settings for the store: Department Code, Default Location Segment, Location Deposit Account and Location Refund Account. If your company uses QuickBooks Online, only Location Refund Account shows, picked from a list of GL accounts (See QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager ). Payment Types : check the Company Payment Types this store can use when paying AP invoices. Web Services : service addresses for the store. These are set by TCS. Do not change them unless TCS Support asks you to. FSM : Factory Schedule Maintenance settings for the store: Add FSM as single Package, Include Inspections, Use Mapped Packages, and Print with Work Order and Print with Invoice (only prints with the initial print). Inventory Locations : enter an Inventory Location for each Sku Type. Available for Retail stores only. Store Hours : enter the store's Open Time, Close Time and Cutoff Time for each Day of Week. Note: Some stores also see End of Day and Key Metrics tabs. These appear only when the feature is turned on for your company."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#misc-settings-tab", "t": "Misc Settings tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Highlight the store, then set these fields. Quotes Commit Inventory : Unchecked by default. Vehicle Tracking : Checked by default. Default Customer ID : Select ... to search for the store's cash customer. TireWorks HD checks that the customer exists in your accounting system. Default Tire Package : Select from the dropdown. See Tire Package Fees . Use Service Appointments : Use if you use the appointment calendar. Transfer Customer ID : Select ... to search for the transfer customer (AR account). Trade Styles : Select from the dropdown if you use them. Tire Tax Sku : Select the ellipsis ( ... ), enter the SKU in the SKU search, and double-click the SKU in the list. Email Configuration : Select SET to set up email for appointments and invoices. See Email Configuration . CheckBookID : Select the checkbook from the dropdown. Pre-populate Count List : Select SKU Types to choose which SKU types fill in counts on this store's inventory count lists. See Physical Inventory Count . Default Price Level : The price level this store uses when the customer has none."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#email-configuration", "t": "Email Configuration", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Use Email Configuration to let each store email service requests, invoices, quick quotes and appointments. You set up email separately for each store. Go to Manage; Location Setup; Locations . Highlight the store. Select the Misc Settings tab. Next to Email Configuration , select Set . In Email Id , enter the email address the store sends from. Each store can have only one email address. In Password , enter the password for that email account. The password is case sensitive. In SMTP Address , enter your email provider's outgoing mail server. Get this from your email provider. In Port , enter the port your email provider gives you. Check Use SSL if your email provider requires it. Under Email For , select each email type (for example Appointment, Invoice and Quick Quote) and edit the Subject , Body and Signature for each. Change the default Subject, Body and Signature text to your company name and information. Customers generally like the store phone number in the Body. Select Preview to see how an HTML email will look. Select Save . Repeat for each store. You don't need to log into each store; highlight each store in the same window. Test by emailing an appointment and an invoice from the store."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#microsoft-365-and-outlook-accounts", "t": "Microsoft 365 and Outlook accounts", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "TCS Support sets up Microsoft 365 and Outlook email accounts that require a Microsoft sign-in. The first time a store sends an email, a Microsoft sign-in window opens. Sign in with the store's email account. Note: Only users with the Outlook Authentication access right can complete the sign-in. Other users see \"Manual Outlook Authentication is Required. Please contact your system administrator.\""}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#asl-tab", "t": "ASL tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "The ASL tab lets a store see other stores' inventory. The application shows inventory for the stores set up here by default, unless the user checks the checkbox to see all locations. Highlight the store. Select stores in the Available Locations list. Select Add to move them from Available Locations to Active ASLs . Hold CTRL to select several stores. Hold SHIFT to select a range of stores. To remove a store from Active ASLs , select Remove . Use the up and down arrows to arrange the stores. Select Save ."}, {"u": "locations-setup-and-maintenance.html#report-disclaimers-tab", "t": "Report Disclaimers tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Locations Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Set reminders or notices by document type. They print at the bottom of every document. Highlight the store. Enter the disclaimer for each document type. The disclaimer prints exactly as typed, so check spelling and punctuation. Select Save ."}, {"u": "customer-classes.html", "t": "Customer classes", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customer classes", "x": "Use customer classes to give a group of customers the same defaults, such as discount percent, tax, shipping method, terms and price level. To open this screen, go to Manage; Company Setup; Customer Class ."}, {"u": "customer-classes.html#add-a-customer-class", "t": "Add a customer class", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customer classes", "x": "Select Add . Under Basic Information , enter the Class ID . Enter the Description . Under Financial Information , enter a Discount Percent if you want one. Under Personal Shipping Info , select a Tax ID from the dropdown. We suggest leaving it blank so sales tax is based on the store performing the service. Select the Shipping Method from the dropdown. This is generally the Will-Call/Pickup method. Select the Terms Code . This is generally CASH SALES. Select the Department code if you use one. Select the Price Level . Review the checkboxes and change them if needed. PO Required is unchecked by default. Active is checked by default. Tire Tax Exempt is unchecked by default. We suggest checking it for National Account classes. Select Save ."}, {"u": "customer-classes.html#edit-a-customer-class", "t": "Edit a customer class", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customer classes", "x": "Highlight the customer class. Make your changes. Select Save ."}, {"u": "customer-classes.html#view-inactive-customer-classes", "t": "View inactive customer classes", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customer classes", "x": "Select . Select ."}, {"u": "customers.html", "t": "Customers", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Use customer setup to create and maintain your Accounts Receivable customers. Customer setup is one of the top three areas where consistency, completeness and accuracy greatly affect your workflow."}, {"u": "customers.html#create-a-customer", "t": "Create a customer", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Go to Manage; Customer . Select the Customer Type . Business is the most common. Enter the customer information to check that the customer doesn't already exist. Existing customers with matching data display under existing customers. Select Create Customer ."}, {"u": "customers.html#general-tab", "t": "General tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "The General tab holds the customer's general information. Fill it in based on your business practices and procedures. Customer Name : The customer's legal name. Customer ID : Fills in automatically unless you choose to override it. Short Name : An abbreviated, searchable name. Customer Type : Check that it's correct. Customer Class : Select from the dropdown list of classes you set up. Status : Active by default. Inactive customers don't display, and setting a customer Inactive also makes all of its members inactive. Hold puts the customer on credit hold. Cash Only hides the Store Account payment method. Customer Since : A calculated field you can't edit. Current Balance : A calculated field imported from your financial software. Salesperson Name : The person responsible for the account. Shipping Method : Select Pickup. Ship Complete Only : Check only if the customer prefers to have the entire order ship at one time. Tax Schedule : Select the tax from the dropdown. The customer is taxable by default unless you choose Exempt. Select No if the default tax rate should be that of the servicing store. Department Code : Select the department code. If you don't use department codes, select 00. Shop Fee Exempt : Check if the customer is exempt. Exempt # : Enter the exemption number if the exemption box is checked. Payment Terms : Select the terms approved by your credit manager. PO Required : Check only if every order must have a PO. Credit Limit : Enter the amount approved by your credit manager. Available for Business customers only. Unused Credit : A calculated field imported from your financial software. Default Price Level : Select the price level from the dropdown. If any of the customer's addresses has its own price level, you're asked \"Would you like to change the price level for all of this customer's addresses?\" Select Yes to update them all. Discount Percentage : Enter a percentage if it applies. Finance Charge : Enter a percentage if it applies. Chain Override Rules : Check if it applies. Show Alert : Check to display an alert dialog box. Alert Message : Free-form field, up to 1000 characters. Comments 1 : Free-form field. Comments 2 : Free-form field. Retread Customer : Check if it applies."}, {"u": "customers.html#members-tab", "t": "Members tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Member information is usually created on the service request, but you can also view, create and maintain it in the customer record. Fill it in if you want."}, {"u": "customers.html#addresses-tab", "t": "Addresses tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "The Addresses tab holds address and pricing information for each address. Address information can be different from the general customer information. Fill it in based on your business practices and procedures. Select Add to add an address, then fill in these fields. Address ID : PRIMARY fills in for the first address. You can change it to any label. You can create multiple addresses. Status : Active by default. Address 1 : The UPS approved address. You can verify an address at www.usps.com. We suggest ALL CAPS and no punctuation. Address 2 : Other address information, such as a PO Box. Postal Code : Enter the zip code. City and State fill in automatically. Required. Country : Select from the dropdown. Check that the city matches the postal service approved city. Website : The customer's website, if they have one. Default Contact : The main contact, if there is one. Default Price Level : Defaults from the General tab. Change it if this address is different. Tax Schedule : Defaults from the General tab. Change it if this address is different. Ignore Customer Pricing : Check if customer pricing should be ignored for this address. Tire Tax Exempt : Check if this address is tire tax exempt."}, {"u": "customers.html#add-contact-information", "t": "Add contact information", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Select Add . Select the Contact Type : NoSet, Email, Fax, Phone, Phone 2 or Text. Selecting Text lets you text the customer from the service request. With two-way texting, replies show in the SMS Hub. See Customer Communication . Enter the phone number. Enter notes if needed. Select Add . Go back to the top of the Addresses tab and fill in the address default information. Enter the right address ID for each."}, {"u": "customers.html#vehicle-tab", "t": "Vehicle tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Vehicle information is usually created on the service request, but you can also view, create and maintain it in the customer record. Fill it in if you want. To add a vehicle, select add (Add New Vehicle), then enter the Plate and Color . Mileage is not entered here. It is recorded on the order. Check Load Inactive Vehicles to include inactive vehicles in the list. In the vehicle's details, the Details area can be collapsed to make more room for the tabs below. On the History tab, select Show Details to see the items on each order. Select Hide Details to go back."}, {"u": "customers.html#customer-rules-tab", "t": "Customer Rules tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "You can set customer price rules at any level of the inventory tree, down to the SKU. A rule set on a branch applies to that branch and every branch and SKU below it. You can also select all items, but then the rule applies to ALL items, including non-inventoried items."}, {"u": "customers.html#create-a-customer-price-rule", "t": "Create a customer price rule", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Select the branch to set the rule on. Use + to open levels. To set the rule on a single SKU, use the Search box. Select the plus sign . The rule level you selected displays in the Rule Detail section. Enter a Name based on the tree branch or SKU the rule is for. Name is required. Select a Class . Cumulative : A chained rule. Additive : Works the same as a cumulative rule. Fixed : Sets a fixed price that overrides price level rules. Margin Ceiling/Margin Floor Round Nearest : Rounds to the nearest value assigned. Round Up : Rounds up to the nearest value assigned. Base Change Rules : Changes the base factor for pricing or cost to something other than the default setting. Matrix : Sets pricing based on a range of price or a range of units. Select an Operand from the dropdown: %, G% or $. The GP% formula is Base/(1.00-GP%). Enter the Value for the operand you selected. Negative values are allowed. Select a Start Date from the calendar if needed. Select an Expiration Date from the calendar if needed. If you don't need an expiration date, leave the default. A new rule's Expiration Date defaults to 15 years from the day it's created. Make sure the rule is checked as active. The finished rule displays in the Customer Pricing Rules section. Select View Prices to check that the rule displays correctly in general inventory search. Select Save when you're done."}, {"u": "customers.html#order-history-tab", "t": "Order History tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "The Order History tab shows all orders for the customer, and lets you see Archived Service History from a previous system. Orders from the Last 30 Days show by default. Use Dates to pick another range, or Custom for your own dates. Select Show Details to see the items on each order. Highlight the order. Select Print or Open Order . Select Archived Service History when you need orders from a previous system."}, {"u": "customers.html#custom-fields-tab-user-defined", "t": "Custom Fields tab (User Defined)", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Use custom fields to store extra information about a customer by address ID, such as program account numbers or tax exempt numbers. Give your administrator the field names and field numbers to create. Each range of field numbers holds one type of data. Fields 1-5 : bit (check box) Fields 6-10 : varchar(50) Fields 11-15 : varchar(200) Fields 16-20 : integer Fields 21-30 : numeric (12,2) Fields 31-35 : datetime"}, {"u": "customers.html#financial-summary-tab", "t": "Financial Summary tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "The Financial Summary tab shows Balance Due, Payment Information and Open Receivables with aging (Future Due, Current, Over 30 to Over 120). Note: This tab isn't shown if your company uses QuickBooks Online or TireBooks."}, {"u": "customers.html#communication-tab", "t": "Communication tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "The Communication tab shows texts and other messages with the customer. See Customer Communication (Texting) . Note: This tab isn't shown for the cash customer."}, {"u": "customers.html#cards-on-file-tab", "t": "Cards On File tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "The Cards On File tab shows the customer's saved cards. See Electronic Payments ."}, {"u": "customers.html#e-commerce-tab", "t": "E-commerce tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "If your company uses the AMI/Mopar integration, use the E-commerce tab to set up each customer's e-commerce details by address. Before you start: TCS sets up the AMI/Mopar integration for your company. You need the Customer Management - eCommerce Tab access right. Under Address E-commerces , select the address. Select Add New E-commerce . Enter the E-commerce Info : E-commerce Identification, Electronic Ordering, Append Orders, Compare PO Number, E-commerce UID, E-commerce Password, Default Sales Location, Second Sales Location, Third Sales Location, Mopar Dealer Code, Ford Dealer Code and GM Dealer Code. Checking Electronic Ordering fills E-commerce UID and E-commerce Password with the Customer ID when they are blank. Important: Selecting Refresh E-commerce List reloads the saved records. Any unsaved changes are lost."}, {"u": "customers.html#ami-mopar-orders", "t": "AMI/Mopar orders", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "When a dealer places an order through AMI/Mopar, TireWorks HD creates an open Service Request for the customer whose Mopar, Ford or GM Dealer Code matches the order. The Service Request is created at that e-commerce record's Default Sales Location . The dealer's order reference is saved as the order's PO number, and the parts and quantities ordered are added as line items. The alert \"New AMI Order received: Service Request [Order ID: ...] has been created for ...\" displays in the SMS Hub. See Customer Communication (Texting) . Open the order from the alert or from the Service Request tab on the Home screen, then work and invoice it like any other Service Request."}, {"u": "customers.html#edit-a-customer-record", "t": "Edit a customer record", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Select Find . Select Customer . Enter the customer information you know. Highlight the customer and select the center icon (a man) to open the customer record."}, {"u": "customers.html#merge-duplicate-customers", "t": "Merge duplicate customers", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customers", "x": "Use Customer Merge to combine a duplicate Household customer into the customer record you want to keep. The duplicate's members, addresses, contacts, vehicles and order history can be moved to the kept customer, and the duplicate is then removed. Before you start: You need the Customer Merge access right. The Customer Merge icon displays only for users who have it. Select Find; Customer and search for the duplicate customer. Hover over the duplicate in the results and select the Customer Merge icon, next to the Customer Details icon. Only Household customers can be merged. Any other type shows \"Please select a valid 'Household' Customer\". At \"Do you want to merge this customer with another household?\", select Yes . The Customer Merge window opens with the duplicate under From (Duplicate) Customer . Under To (Base) Customer , select Select... and choose the customer to keep. It must be a different customer. Use the Members , Addresses and Vehicle tabs to bring over what you want to keep. The duplicate's items are on one side and the kept customer's items are on the other. Move : Moves the selected member, address or vehicle to the kept customer. Merge (Members and Addresses): Moves the orders of the selected duplicate member or address onto the selected member or address of the kept customer. Replace (Vehicle): Replaces the kept customer's selected vehicle with the duplicate's selected vehicle. Copy Order (Vehicle): Moves the orders of the duplicate's selected vehicle onto the kept customer's selected vehicle. Contacts : Select a contact and select Move to add it to the selected member or address of the kept customer. Select Save , then select Yes at the confirmation. The confirmation warns \"This process is not reversible.\" When the merge finishes, \"Customer Id : [Id] was successfully merged.\" displays. Important: After a merge, the duplicate customer no longer exists. Comments 2 on the kept customer records which Customer Id was merged into it and when."}, {"u": "customer-contract-pricing.html", "t": "Customer (contract) pricing", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Customer (contract) pricing", "x": "Use customer rules to set pricing for one customer, on top of the price level assigned in the customer record or the store's default price level. On the Home screen, select FIND and make sure Customers shows in Look For: . Select the Advanced Search tab. Enter any of Customer Name , Customer Type , Created Date or Customer Trade Style , then select Search . You don't need to fill in every field. Select Customer Details , to the left of CustomerId . In the customer record, select the CUSTOMER RULES tab. Note: You can set customer price rules at any level of the inventory tree, down to the SKU. A rule set on a branch applies to that branch and every branch and SKU below it. You can also select all items, but then the rule applies to ALL items, including non-inventoried items. Select the branch to set the rule on, or go to the bottom of the inventory tree and search for a specific SKU. Then select the plus sign under Rule Details . The tree structure for your rule displays in Rule Details . You need to open the branches yourself. Fill in the rule fields. Rule Name : A name based on the tree branch or SKU the rule is for. Class : Select one of these. Cumulative : A chained rule. Additive : Works the same as a cumulative rule. Fixed : Sets a fixed price that overrides price level rules. Margin Ceiling/Margin Floor Round Nearest : Rounds to the nearest value assigned. Round Up : Rounds up to the nearest value assigned. Base Change Rules : Changes the base factor for pricing or cost to something other than the default setting. Matrix : Sets pricing based on a range of price or a range of units. Operand : Select %, G% or $. The GP% formula is Base/(1.00-GP%). Value : Enter the value for the operand you selected. Negative values are allowed. Start Date : Select the dropdown and choose the start date. Exp. Date : Select the dropdown and choose the expiration date. If you don't need an expiration date, leave the default. A new rule's Exp. Date defaults to 15 years from the day it's created. Active : Make sure it's checked for active status. Note: These fields fill in automatically as you enter the information above. Select View Prices to check that the rule displays correctly in general inventory search. Select Save when you're done."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html", "t": "Discount Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "Use the Manage Discounts and Coupons window to set up discount reason codes and coupon campaigns. It has many options so you can fit each discount to your business needs. Before you start: You need the Company Setup - Discounts and Coupons access right. To open this window, go to Manage; Company Setup and open Manage Discounts and Coupons . The General tab of the Discount Reason Codes window holds the options shown here. Use the Discount Reason Codes and Coupon Campaigns radio buttons at the top to choose what you're setting up. Coupon Campaigns use the same window. Select Coupon Campaigns to set up coupon codes. You can set Allow Duplicate Coupons and a coupon number pattern of Left Characters , Right Characters , Starting Number and Ending Number . Note: Auto Apply and Buy 3 Get 1 Free are for discounts only."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#discount-reason-code-fields", "t": "Discount reason code fields", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "A new discount reason code needs a Discount Code , a Description , and whether it's Active . The other fields are optional. Hover over the icons in the window to see information about each option. The optional fields are: Discount Type : Sets a default discount type, Flat Discount or Percent Discount. You can change it when you apply the discount to a Service Request. Amount : Sets a default amount. You can change it when you apply the discount to a Service Request. Start Date & End Date : Set the dates when the discount can be added to a Service Request. The discount can't be added outside that date range. Note: An order that already has a discount keeps it after the End Date passes, until payment. At Add Payment , TireWorks HD checks the order for expired or inactive discounts and coupons. Users with the Service Request - Expired Discount access right can choose to keep them. For other users they're removed and the order total changes. Check Honor After Expiration to skip this check for the discount. Auto Apply : Check to have the application apply the discount automatically based on the configured Discount Restrictions. Note: We strongly recommend setting up specific restrictions when you turn on Auto Apply. Otherwise the application applies the discount to every item. Allow Once per Invoice : When checked, the discount reason code can be added to a Service Request only once. A second attempt shows \"This discount reason is allowed only once on an invoice. Please edit the already added one OR remove that and add a new one.\" Auto Apply discounts also honor Allow Once per Invoice when several packages on the order qualify. Buy 3 Get 1 Free : When checked, Discount Type and Amount can't be edited. This option is designed for tires. With or without Restrictions, you can add it only to eligible tires with a quantity of 4 or more. The application calculates the price of a single unit and puts it in the discount amount on the line item. Note: You can't edit the amount or discount type of a Buy 3 Get 1 Free discount. It's calculated automatically from the tire's unit price, and it applies only when the quantity is 4 or more. If you reduce the quantity, the application removes the discount. If a user hand prices the tire after the discount is applied, the application updates the discount to the correct amount. The FetDiscountable System Setting also affects the amount. When it's True, the calculated discount is Price + FET. When it's False, the calculated discount is Price. Nitrogen Discountable : Sets whether Nitrogen is discountable. This applies to the SKU set up as the Nitrogen SKU code on the Nitrogen Items tab of the Manage; Company Setup; Other Fees and Charges window. Note: You can't enter negative amounts for discounts and coupons. Minimum Qty : Works only with Inventory or Sku Type restrictions. The discount is split equally across the qualifying line items. Editable on Service Request : When checked, the discount amount and type can be edited on the Service Request. When unchecked, they can't. Per Unit : The discount must be applied to a line item using a Package or Inventory restriction. A flat discount is applied per unit. Class : Discounts and coupons of the same class, or with no class, can be combined. When discounts of different classes qualify on the same package, the one with the largest discount for the customer is applied. Road Hazard Discountable : Sets whether Road Hazard is discountable. This applies to the SKU set up as the Road Hazard SKU code on the Road Hazard Items tab of the Manage; Company Setup; Other Fees and Charges window."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#discount-restrictions", "t": "Discount restrictions", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "Use Discount Restrictions to make a discount eligible only under certain conditions. See the image below, or open the Restrictions in the Manage Discounts window, for the available restrictions. To set restrictions, open the Manage Discounts window from the Manage; Company Setup menu. The window has two tabs. The General tab is covered in Discount reason code fields above. This section covers how Restrictions work and how to set them up. Restrictions are completely optional. They give you more control over who, what, where and when the discount can be applied. There are 7 restrictions you can configure: Locations, Sku Types, Customer Classes, Packages, Inventory, Price Level and Customers. If no restrictions are configured, the discount can be used anywhere, on anything, for anyone. This keeps discounts backward compatible with the discounts functionality in previous versions. Note: The Restrictions tab has a scroll bar on the right that grows as you expand restrictions. You may see two vertical scroll bars: the outer one moves between restrictions, and the inner one scrolls the options within a restriction. For example, the Inventory restriction shows the whole inventory tree with its own scroll bar, while the outer scroll bar lets you scroll up to the Location restrictions."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#locations", "t": "Locations", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "Expand Locations . To show only stores assigned to one region, filter the list by Regions . Select specific stores, or select Select All , to restrict the discount to those stores. Select Save so your changes aren't lost."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#sku-types", "t": "SKU Types", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "Expand SKU Types . Use the filter box to find SKU types without scrolling. Select any or all of the SKU types you want the discount to be eligible on. Select Save so your changes aren't lost. Note: With a SKU Type restriction, where you place the discount determines how it's applied. For example, you set up a SKU Type restriction for Tires with a $5 discount. If you add the discount at the Service Request or Package level, it applies to every item of that SKU type: 3 Tire line items get (3) $5 discounts, for a total discount of $15. If you add the same discount to one Tire line item, it results in (1) $5 discount."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#customer-classes", "t": "Customer Classes", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "In Customer Classes , select the customer classes eligible for this discount. Use the Look For filter box or Select All . Select Save so your changes aren't lost."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#packages", "t": "Packages", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "The Packages restriction is more complex than selecting an eligible store. You choose not only which package is eligible but also which line items in the package are eligible. Highlight the package. To include all of its line items, select Select All . Select Add . The package and its line items show as eligible in the Configured Packages section, below the list of Packages. To remove eligibility, use a delete icon in Configured Packages . The icon on the right removes specific line items, and the icon on the left removes the entire package. Select Save so your changes aren't lost."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#inventory", "t": "Inventory", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "The Inventory restriction shows the inventory tree. You can make an item eligible for the discount in two ways. Inventory Tree : Drill down in the tree, select a tree node or SKU, and select >> to add it to the right side. Search On : Look up items using the available search options. For example, search for \"Passenger\" on the \"Class\" tree level. Then select Select All , or choose the specific passenger classes you want to make eligible. You can remove items in two ways. Delete icons : Select an item's delete icon to remove that item from the eligible inventory restrictions. Delete button : Click each item you want to remove, then select Delete at the bottom. Confirm the deletion when prompted. Select Save so your changes aren't lost."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#price-level", "t": "Price Level", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "The Price Level restriction limits the discount to customers on the price levels you check. Use the Look For filter box or Select All . Select Save so your changes aren't lost."}, {"u": "discount-maintenance.html#customers", "t": "Customers", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Discount Maintenance", "x": "The Customers restriction limits the discount to specific customers. Select Search and Add Customer to find and add each customer. To remove one, use the delete icon and confirm when prompted. Select Save so your changes aren't lost."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html", "t": "Inventory Management", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Use Inventory Management to create and manage inventory items, define price levels and rule assignments, maintain cost and base value fields, manage tire fee states, view item detail from TDC (Tire Data Central), and keep any additional item information you want. Go to Manage; Inventory; Manage Inventory ."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#the-inventory-tree", "t": "The inventory tree", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "The inventory tree has six levels for tires, parts, retreads, wheels, non-inventoried items and more. The shared tree structure keeps items consistent, which makes reporting more effective. TDC item : The item is housed in TDC (Tire Data Central). Local item : The item was created locally. Items in red : The item is inactive. Manufacturer : The manufacturer name, such as Michelin. Sub-Manufacturer : Groups several brands under one manufacturer, such as Michelin, BF Goodrich and Uniroyal. Class : The tire type, such as passenger, light truck or medium truck. Sub-Class : The tire type, such as all season, all terrain or touring. Category : The tire line, such as Ecopia, Destination AT or FR380. Sub-Category : Additional information about the tire line. This is typically set as Default."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#find-an-item", "t": "Find an item", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Use the + and - symbols to open levels of the tree, or enter an item number to go straight to the item. Enter the item number and select Search SKU ."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#item-detail-tab", "t": "Item Detail tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "The Item Detail tab draws on a tire database of over 105,000 items for tire specifications, pictures, comparisons, features and warranty information. You can print this information or email it from the inventory search screen. User Sku Code : Enter the SKU code you want. This is generally the item number from your previous software. Item Group Selection : Select an item group from the Item Group dropdown. See Item Group Setup and Item Assignment . Program Product Codes : Assigns the program item number required for submission. To add a program product code: Select Add New . Select the program from the Program dropdown. Enter the National Account product code. Select Done . Note: To delete a line item, select . Note: When you change Outside Purchase SKU , you are asked whether the change applies to all locations or this location only."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#inactivate-an-item", "t": "Inactivate an item", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Clear the Active check box. The item no longer displays in search results."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#pricing-tab", "t": "Pricing tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Use the Pricing tab to set and maintain price rules within the price levels you created, based on any level of the inventory tree."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#create-a-price-rule", "t": "Create a price rule", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Select the branch where you want to set the rule. Use + to open levels. To set the rule on a single SKU, use the Search box to select it. Select Add Rule . The branch or item you selected displays in the Rule From column. A rule set at a branch affects all branches and items below that branch. Select the Price Level the rule applies to. Enter a Name based on the tree branch or SKU the rule was created for. This field is required. Select the Type . Select %, G% or $. The GP% formula is Base/(1.00-GP%). Select the Class . Cumulative : A chained rule. Additive : Works the same way as a cumulative rule. Fixed : Sets a fixed price that overrides price level rules. Margin Ceiling/Margin Floor Round Nearest : Rounds to the nearest value assigned. Round Up : Rounds up to the nearest value assigned. Base Change Rules : Changes the base factor for pricing or cost to something other than the default setting. Matrix : Sets pricing based on a range of price or a range of units. If you want Matrix pricing, enter Min Cost and Max Cost . Enter the Value for the type and class you selected. Negative values are allowed. Use the Move Up and Move Down icons to arrange the rule order. Price rules are chained. Select Save ."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#remove-a-price-rule", "t": "Remove a price rule", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Select the rule you want to delete. Select . Select Save ."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#site-detail-tab", "t": "Site Detail tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "The Site Detail tab shows quantities on hand, committed and ordered, along with last cost and average cost. You can also enter, edit or load the fields shown in white. Last Cost and Average Cost : Only users with the Item - Edit Last Cost and Item - Edit Average Cost access rights can edit these. Is Inventoried : Changes whether the item is inventoried at this store. After a SKU is saved, the Inventoried box on the Item Detail tab can't be changed. Base Value Fields (20) : Editable, loadable fields you can use for a price level base, default pricing and more. True Cost , Invoice Cost , Calc Cost 1 and Calc Cost 2 : Editable, loadable fields you can use for a price level base, for the default cost on invoices, purchase orders, adjustments and receipts, or both. Min/Max Reorder Points : Editable, loadable fields that set reorder requirements. Tip: You can edit all stores from one screen by selecting the store in the Site Detail Location dropdown ."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#other-tabs", "t": "Other tabs", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "User Defined : Provides 35 additional informational fields that you can title and fill in, for report use only. They include check box, character, integer and date fields. You might use them for data such as equivalencies if you use integrated routing software. Item History : Gives an overview of the item's history for the previous 12 months. By month, it shows total sales dollars, sales units, sales average dollars, GP average dollars, receipt dollars, receipt quantity, receipts average dollars and receipts % change dollars. Units of Measure : Sets additional units of measure and assigns them to multiple order types or modules. You can also define dimension and weight settings here. Core : Shows only if your company uses parts cores. Sets whether the item is a core or has a core. On Order : Lists outstanding purchase orders and inbound transfers for the item. Item Allocation : Lists the orders the item is allocated to, with Location, Type, Order #, Customer, Status and Qty Allocated. Item Movement : Lists the item's transactions for the Dates you pick, with Trans. Type, Trans #, Cost, Qty and Snapshot Qty. Note: If you leave the window, move in the inventory tree, or pick another SKU while you have unsaved changes, you are asked to save, discard or cancel."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#add-a-branch-or-item", "t": "Add a branch or item", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Select the branch above where you want the new branch or item. Use + to open the tree to the branch you want. Select the arrow for what you want to add. The blue arrow adds a new branch. The green arrow adds a new item."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#add-a-branch", "t": "Add a branch", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Select the blue arrow. Select Add New Category . Enter the Category Name and Short Lookup . Select Save ."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#add-an-item", "t": "Add an item", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Open the tree to the branch where the item belongs, as described above. Select the green arrow. Select Add New Sku . Enter the Universal Sku , which has three segments. The simple tire size, such as 2656016, with no symbols or letters. The 3-digit manufacturer SKU, such as MIC. This is generally three characters, with a few exceptions. The manufacturer item number. Enter the Manufacturer Sku . Enter a Description . Include as much detail as you can, because this field is searchable. Enter Dealer Base if you use it. Enter FET if the tire meets the criteria. Select an End Date from the calendar. We suggest using the same future date on all new SKUs. The End Date defines whether the product is discontinued. A discontinued item displays in red in inventory search. Enter User Sku if you use it. Enter the Short Sku Code . Select the Sku Type . This helps with reporting, shop fee setup and more. If the item is a fluid, select the Fluid Type . Select an Item Group from the dropdown if you use item groups. Review the check boxes. Active is checked by default unless you change it. Taxable , Inventoried and Tech Required are checked by default. Clear any that don't apply. You can change Inventoried on this screen only while the SKU is new. After you save it, change it on the Site Detail tab. Select Save . Note: Always fill in the Site Detail tab when you create or load new items, and check whether the item also needs pricing setup. See Site Detail tab and Pricing tab above. A tire SKU can't be saved until its required tire fields are filled in. A message tells you what is missing."}, {"u": "inventory-management.html#set-up-sku-types", "t": "Set up SKU types", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Inventory Management", "x": "Use SKU types to classify items for reporting, shop fee setup and more. Go to Manage; Company Setup; Sku Types . Select Add , and then enter the Description and Line Item Type . You can set the Description and Line Item Type only while the SKU type is new. To let users edit the description of items of this SKU type on a Service Request, check Allow User to Edit the Item Description on Service Requests (for California BAR compliance). Users with the Service Request - Item Description access right can edit any item description, whatever the SKU type setting. Select Save ."}, {"u": "item-group-setup-and-item-assignment.html", "t": "Item Group Setup and Item Assignment", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Item Group Setup and Item Assignment", "x": "Use item groups to display inventory by group in a general search. You can give each group a color and rank the groups in display order. You set groups up once, and they cover all stores. Go to Manage; Inventory; Item Group ."}, {"u": "item-group-setup-and-item-assignment.html#create-an-item-group", "t": "Create an item group", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Item Group Setup and Item Assignment", "x": "Select Add . On the Item Group Details tab, enter the Item Group Name . Enter a Description . Select a Start Date from the calendar . If you want one, select an End Date from the calendar . Select a color for the group's items to display in. Turn Set Priority as Nothing on or off as needed. Turn Show Always on or off as needed. Select Save . \"Successfully Saved\" displays. The group now displays in the Item Group List ."}, {"u": "item-group-setup-and-item-assignment.html#add-skus-on-the-sku-itemgroup-mapping-tab", "t": "Add SKUs on the Sku ItemGroup Mapping tab", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Item Group Setup and Item Assignment", "x": "The Sku ItemGroup Mapping tab lists the SKUs in the selected group and lets you add SKUs to it. In Search Item to Add , enter at least three characters of the SKU and select Search . If more than one item matches, select the item from the list. To create a new SKU, select Create Item . This requires the Inventory Management access right. Select Save . Note: You can also add items to a group from Manage Inventory. See Add items to a group below."}, {"u": "item-group-setup-and-item-assignment.html#rank-item-groups", "t": "Rank item groups", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Item Group Setup and Item Assignment", "x": "Select a group and use to move it into the display order you want."}, {"u": "item-group-setup-and-item-assignment.html#add-items-to-a-group", "t": "Add items to a group", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Item Group Setup and Item Assignment", "x": "Go to Manage; Inventory; Manage Inventory . Enter the Manufacturer Item Number , select the SKU from the results list, and select OK . On the Item Detail tab, select the group from the dropdown shown below. Select Save . \"Successfully Saved\" displays."}, {"u": "create-a-part.html", "t": "Create a part", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Create a part", "x": "Use Create Part to create and manage items you order through outside purchase, such as original equipment parts. These parts become inventoried items and are priced by the price rules of the branch the item is placed in. Select Item Lookup . Search for the part number to make sure it isn't already in inventory management. Select Create Part . Manufacturer is fixed to Parts, Labor & Service. Sub-manufacturer through Sub-category come in with defaults, but you can choose others. Important: These selections decide where the item is created in the inventory tree, which drives pricing and GL posting in QB. Select Next . Enter the original equipment item number. The item number copies into the description automatically. Overwrite it with the description you want. Enter the Cost . This cost passes to the service request, PO, receipt and AP invoice. Enter the Price . It defaults above cost until you overwrite it. Enter the Quantity . If there are multiple packages on the order, select the package to add the item to. Select Create Part . The part is added to the order automatically, with a sourcing icon. Source and receive the part as usual. Note: This process creates the item in the right branch of the inventory master file. Because it is an inventoried item, it now shows on the unsold purchases report, and you can either return an unsold item or put it away. Returning it creates a credit AP invoice."}, {"u": "labor-rate-setup-and-maintenance.html", "t": "Labor Rate Setup and Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Labor Rate Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Use Labor Rate to set the hourly labor rate for each skill level. Each skill level holds its own labor rate, set by store. Before you start: Access to Manage functions is controlled by access rights. Go to Manage; Location Setup; Labor Rate . Log in to the store you want to set rates for. To copy this store's labor rates to other stores, use Copy Labor Rate . Select each skill level. Enter or change the hourly Labor Rate . Select Save when you're done. Select the red X to close the labor rate screen."}, {"u": "order-validation.html", "t": "Order Validation", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Order Validation", "x": "Use Order Validation to decide which information users must collect, or are prompted to collect, before a customer is billed out. Go to Manage; Location Setup; Order Validation ."}, {"u": "order-validation.html#set-validation-conditions", "t": "Set validation conditions", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Order Validation", "x": "For each Condition , pick IGNORE , WARN or BLOCK under each order state: Quick Quote, Appointment, Estimate, Work Order, Work Complete, Invoice, Declined and Cancelled. Setting WARN or BLOCK at one state also sets it for the states after it. This is typically set at Invoice, so users have time to fill in the information as the order moves along, up until it is invoiced. Conditions are listed alphabetically. Some conditions show only when the feature they belong to is turned on for your company. Ignore : Doesn't require or suggest that the information is collected. Warn : Suggests that the user collect the information, but doesn't require it. Shown by on the service request. Block : Requires the information before invoicing. Shown by on the service request. Select Save ."}, {"u": "order-validation.html#copy-order-validation-to-other-stores", "t": "Copy order validation to other stores", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Order Validation", "x": "If you have multiple stores, you can copy your order validation settings to all other stores or to specific ones. Select Copy Order Validation . Select in the Filter: Region box and choose Select All . Clear any stores you don't want to copy to. Select Copy ."}, {"u": "order-validation.html#check-order-validation-on-a-service-request", "t": "Check order validation on a service request", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Order Validation", "x": "Order Validation Status is in the top right corner of a service request. It shows the same icons as above, plus when all conditions are met and the order is ready to invoice. In this window, select the fix icon to fill in the information without going back to find it in the service request. When you save or invoice, the Order Validation and Prompts window lists anything still open. See Order Prompts . You can fix blocked validations from this window at the time of invoicing."}, {"u": "physical-inventory-count.html", "t": "Physical Inventory Count", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Physical Inventory Count", "x": "Use Physical Inventory Count to take a snapshot of current inventory, print a count book for a manual count or scan inventory, run a variance report, and create and process the inventory adjustment automatically. Go to Manage; Inventory; Advance Physical Inventory Count; Inventory Snapshot ."}, {"u": "physical-inventory-count.html#create-an-inventory-snapshot", "t": "Create an inventory snapshot", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Physical Inventory Count", "x": "Select the store in the location list. Only stores where you have the Adv. Inv. Count - Inventory Snapshot access right are listed. Enter a Snapshot Name , such as the store number and date. To snapshot only specific SKU types, check Partial Snapshot? and select the SKU types. Select types in Available SKU Types and select . Hold CTRL to select several. Hold SHIFT to select a range. Select Done . Check Pre-populate Count List? if you want. Counts fill in only for items with a quantity on hand. If you leave it unchecked, counts start blank. Select SKU Types . Select types in Available SKU Types and select . Hold CTRL to select several. Hold SHIFT to select a range. Select Done . Select . The snapshot list displays automatically. Select Back to return to the Inventory Snapshot screen. After the snapshot is saved, more options display: : Discards the snapshot. : Processes the inventory adjustment."}, {"u": "physical-inventory-count.html#option-1-print-manual-count-sheets", "t": "Option 1: Print manual count sheets", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Physical Inventory Count", "x": "Select . Enter filter information and sort orders if you want. Is Stocked? : This is the not inventoried check box. QOH for the Item >0 : Makes the list shorter, but may mean more items written in by hand that would have been on the list if you left it unchecked. Items sold/ordered within the past XX month(s) Set sort orders by SKU type. One icon deletes a sort item from the list. One icon changes the sort order. Check For All Other Sku Types if not all SKU types are listed. Select to add sort items. Use to move SKU types into the order you want. Select Print . Select Print in the report window."}, {"u": "physical-inventory-count.html#option-2-use-count-lists", "t": "Option 2: Use count lists", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Physical Inventory Count", "x": "Go to Manage; Inventory; Advance Physical Inventory Count; Inventory Count Lists . Enter a Name and Description , and select Create CountList . Open the count list and enter each item's Actual Count . A blank count is skipped. A 0 is counted and included in the variance. Select Save to keep working later, or Submit when the count list is done."}, {"u": "physical-inventory-count.html#process-the-snapshot", "t": "Process the snapshot", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Physical Inventory Count", "x": "On the Inventory Snapshot screen, select the snapshot and print the Inventory Variance Report . Select Process . You must print the variance report first. You must submit or delete every count list first. Processing updates quantity on hand and inventory valuation for the store. Note: The QOH column in the snapshot's Inventory Items list shows only for users with the Adv. Inv. Count - Inventory Snapshot – QOH access right. Note: To print a Physical Inventory Count Report for All Items or selected inventory tree branches without creating a snapshot, go to Manage; Inventory; Physical Inventory Count ."}, {"u": "cycle-count-setup-and-maintenance.html", "t": "Cycle Count Setup and Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Cycle Count Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Use cycle counts to set up stores for counting based on SKU types, turns and more. Cycle counts populate automatically for each store on the days of the week you set. Cycle count setup is under Manage; Inventory; Advanced Physical Inventory Count , in Cycle Count Filter and Cycle Count Filters for Location ."}, {"u": "cycle-count-setup-and-maintenance.html#set-up-a-cycle-count-filter", "t": "Set up a cycle count filter", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Cycle Count Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Go to Manage; Inventory; Advanced Physical Inventory Count; Cycle Count Filter . Select . Enter the Count Filter Name . Enter the number of Turns , generally 1. This is how many times to count within the date range you select. Enter a Description to explain the filter name if needed. Select the inventory you expect to count from the inventory tree. Select All Items if you plan to select by SKU types. Or select the branches you want at any level of the inventory tree. Select to add them to the Selected Nodes list. Check the SKU types you want, or check Select All Sku Types . If you select all SKU types, the results include items that aren't inventoried, such as labor, fees and other charges. Select Save ."}, {"u": "cycle-count-setup-and-maintenance.html#assign-cycle-count-filters-to-stores", "t": "Assign cycle count filters to stores", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Cycle Count Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Go to Manage; Inventory; Advanced Physical Inventory Count; Cycle Count Filters for Location . Select the store or stores. Select the filter or filters. Check the Count Days you want. Select Add . The assignment displays under Active Location Filter Assignments . Select the stores to generate a schedule for. Select . Select the date range of the cycle count period. Press Enter or double-click the selected date to accept the dates. A dialog box asks you to verify the stores and date range. Select Yes or No . A second dialog box confirms that the cycle count was generated. Select OK . Stores set up for cycle counting now have a CYCLE COUNT tab on the home screen. See Complete a cycle count below for the steps users follow."}, {"u": "cycle-count-setup-and-maintenance.html#complete-a-cycle-count", "t": "Complete a cycle count", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Cycle Count Setup and Maintenance", "x": "The CYCLE COUNT tab shows all cycle counts for the date range and number of turns selected. You can print a count, or open it with the icon to the left of the line. Count the product physically, following your company's business practice. Open the schedule ID you counted, using the icon to the left of the ID number. Enter the quantities counted in the Qty. Counted column. The Variance column shows the counted quantity less current QOH. Change the User ID if there were multiple counters. Enter comments if you want. Select Save or Process , depending on your business process. Save keeps the count for processing later. Process generates an inventory adjustment automatically. If you chose Process , confirm when you are asked to process the cycle count. A dialog box displays when it processes successfully. To find the adjustment, go to Find; Inventory Adjustment . Its comments show that it was created from a cycle count, and the date. Note: Clear if you don't want processed cycle counts to display on the CYCLE COUNT tab."}, {"u": "cycle-count-setup-and-maintenance.html#maintain-store-assignments", "t": "Maintain store assignments", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Cycle Count Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Make these changes on Cycle Count Filters for Location . To remove a store: Hover over the store. Select the minus sign to the left of the store name. To delete a cycle count schedule: Select the stores. Select . Select the changed dates and follow the setup steps above. To change the days of the week: Select the ellipsis to the right of the store. Change the days. Select OK ."}, {"u": "cycle-count-setup-and-maintenance.html#maintain-cycle-count-filters", "t": "Maintain cycle count filters", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Cycle Count Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Make these changes on Cycle Count Filter . To edit or open a filter: Select the green arrow to the left of the filter name. Make your changes. Select Save . To delete a filter: Select the minus sign to the left of the filter name. Select Yes or No in the dialog box. Select Save ."}, {"u": "payment-setup.html", "t": "Payment Setup", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Payment Setup", "x": "Set up payment terms in Manage; Company Setup; Payment Terms . Set up credit card terminals in Manage; Location Setup; Credit Card Terminals . See Electronic Payments ."}, {"u": "payment-setup.html#set-up-payment-terms", "t": "Set up payment terms", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Payment Setup", "x": "The payment terms you set up here are the choices in Payment Terms on customers (General tab), customer classes, purchase orders, inventory receipts and AP invoices. Before you start: Saving changes requires the Manage - Payment Terms access right. Without it, \"You do not have permission to save data.\" displays. Go to Manage; Company Setup; Payment Terms . The list shows each Payment Term Code . Use Look For to filter by Terms Code. Select Add New Payment Term . Enter the Terms Code Id and Terms Code Display . Both are required, and each Terms Code Id can be used only once. Complete any other fields your business uses: Due Type , Due Date Days , Disc. Type , Disc. Date Days , Disc. Calc. Type , Disc. Amount , Disc. Percent , Sales Purchase , Disc. CB , Freight , Misc , Tax , Proxy Day , Proxy Day Disc. , Term 1 through Term 4 , Cutoff Day and Payment Type . Select Save . \"Save Successful\" displays. If your company uses accounting integration, saved terms are also sent to your accounting package."}, {"u": "payment-setup.html#delete-a-payment-term", "t": "Delete a payment term", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Payment Setup", "x": "Select the term. Select the delete icon. Select Yes at \"Are you sure to delete this Payment Term?\" Note: A term that is already in use can't be deleted. A message explains why."}, {"u": "payment-setup.html#how-payment-terms-set-ap-invoice-due-dates", "t": "How payment terms set AP invoice due dates", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Payment Setup", "x": "When an AP invoice uses a term with a Proxy Day , its due date falls on that day of the month. Due Date Days sets how far out, counted in 30-day months. An invoice dated on or after the Cutoff Day moves one more month out."}, {"u": "price-level-setup-and-maintenance.html", "t": "Price Level Setup and Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Price Level Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Use price levels to set default prices by customer, by store, or both. You can create as many levels as you need. Go to Manage; Company Setup; Pricing ."}, {"u": "price-level-setup-and-maintenance.html#add-a-price-level", "t": "Add a price level", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Price Level Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Select . Enter a Name . Select a Parent . This makes another price level the parent. All the parent's price rules are copied to the new level. When the parent price level changes, all its child price levels change too. Make sure Active is checked. It's checked by default. Select ."}, {"u": "price-level-setup-and-maintenance.html#edit-a-price-level", "t": "Edit a price level", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Price Level Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Select the price level you want to edit. Make your changes. Select ."}, {"u": "price-level-setup-and-maintenance.html#inactivate-a-price-level", "t": "Inactivate a price level", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Price Level Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Select the price level you want to inactivate. Clear the Active box. Select ."}, {"u": "quickbooks-online-and-the-integration-manager.html", "t": "QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "p": "Section 6: Manage › QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "x": "When your company uses QuickBooks Online (QBO), TireWorks HD sends your invoices, returns, customer payments, customer deposits, vendor bills, inventory receipts, and inventory adjustments to QBO. Customers, vendors, GL accounts, tax details, payment terms, payment types, credit cards, and customer classes are kept in step between the two systems. Note: TCS connects TireWorks HD to your QBO company and turns on the Integration Manager during setup. Contact TCS Support for the first connection, or if QBO asks you to sign in again and you don't have access to finish it."}, {"u": "quickbooks-online-and-the-integration-manager.html#where-accounting-errors-show-up", "t": "Where accounting errors show up", "p": "Section 6: Manage › QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "x": "Closing an invoice no longer stops to show an accounting error. The invoice closes and prints as normal. If the invoice did not reach QBO, it waits in Integration Manager with the reason attached. Note: Check Integration Manager daily so nothing sits unposted."}, {"u": "quickbooks-online-and-the-integration-manager.html#check-sync-status", "t": "Check sync status", "p": "Section 6: Manage › QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "x": "Go to Manage; Utilities; Accounting Integration . Select the Integration Manager tab. Check the stores to review, or check All Locations . Check the document types to review, or check All DocumentTypes . The list shows every document that has not integrated yet, with Location , Doc Type , Doc Number , In Process , Trans Date and Last Attempt . Total Items shows how many are waiting. Select the refresh icon to reload the list. Note: Integration Manager remembers the stores and document types you picked last time."}, {"u": "quickbooks-online-and-the-integration-manager.html#fix-a-failed-item", "t": "Fix a failed item", "p": "Section 6: Manage › QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "x": "Double-click the document, or right-click it and select View Messages , to read why it failed. Correct the cause. Common causes are a customer class, item or account that is missing in QBO, or a record in QBO that is missing required information. Select the document and select Re-Integrate Selection . Use Ctrl + Click to pick several documents, Shift + Click for a range, or Ctrl + A for all. If you made the fix to the TireWorks HD record itself, select Rebuild And Re-Integrate Selection instead. This rebuilds the accounting data from the document before sending it again. Select Yes at \"Do you really want to rebuild the accounting data before re-integrating the selected documents?\" Requires the Accounting Integration - Rebuild XML access right. Note: If a document shows In Process and never finishes, right-click it and select Reset In Progress flag , and then re-integrate it. Note: TireWorks HD checks QBO for an existing inventory receipt, adjustment or AP invoice with the same document number before sending, so re-integrating doesn't create a duplicate."}, {"u": "quickbooks-online-and-the-integration-manager.html#sync-records-with-qbo", "t": "Sync records with QBO", "p": "Section 6: Manage › QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "x": "Use Sync Items to pull setup records from QBO, or push records to QBO, on demand. Select the Integration tab, and then Sync Items . At Sync Direction , select Receive (from QBO) or Send (to QBO). At Items To Sync , select the record type: Credit Cards, Customer Classes, Customers, GL Accounts, Payment Terms, Payment Types, Tax Schedules or Vendors. Send lists only the record types turned on under Integration Options on the General tab. To only link unmatched records and create missing ones, check Sync Unsynced Items Only (No Updates) . Uncheck it to also update records that are already linked. This can take a long time. Select Receive Items or Send Items . Review the Log . To copy the log for Support, select the copy icon. Note: A QBO record missing required information is skipped, and the log names it. Complete the record in QBO and sync again."}, {"u": "quickbooks-online-and-the-integration-manager.html#set-up-tax-variance-alerts", "t": "Set up tax variance alerts", "p": "Section 6: Manage › QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "x": "TireWorks HD can compare the tax QBO calculates on a posted invoice with the tax TireWorks HD calculated, and alert you when they differ. The invoice still posts. The alert is for review. Select the General tab and go to Tax Variance Alerts . Check Enable Tax Variance Alerts . Enter a Dollar Variance Threshold , a Percent Variance Threshold , or both. Going over either one creates an alert. Select Save . Note: You can't save with the alerts turned on and both thresholds blank."}, {"u": "quickbooks-online-and-the-integration-manager.html#review-integration-alerts", "t": "Review integration alerts", "p": "Section 6: Manage › QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "x": "Before you start: The Integration Alerts tab appears only after Tax Variance Alerts is turned on. Select the Integration Alerts tab. A red count on the tab shows unread alerts. Filter by Location and Document Type if needed. The grid shows Location , Doc. Type , Doc. Number , Txn Tax Details , Alert Message and Date/Time . Select one or more alerts and select Mark as read . You don't need to save."}, {"u": "quickbooks-online-and-the-integration-manager.html#screens-that-work-differently-with-qbo", "t": "Screens that work differently with QBO", "p": "Section 6: Manage › QuickBooks Online and the Integration Manager", "x": "GL Account : Display only. Add or change GL accounts in QBO, and then receive them on Sync Items. Customer Maintenance : The Financial Summary tab isn't shown. Manage Tax Details : You must select a Tax Agency before you can save a new tax detail. After the first save, Tax Detail ID , Tax Agency , Tax Detail Type and Tax Detail Percent can't be changed. Manage Locations, Accounting tab : Choose the Location Refund Account from the list. Fields that don't apply to QBO are hidden. Customers and vendors : Appear in QBO as NAME (ID), so two with the same name stay separate."}, {"u": "system-settings.html", "t": "System Settings", "p": "Section 6: Manage › System Settings", "x": "Use System Settings to control how your company and each store behave, including defaults, optional rules and integrations. Many features are turned on here. Before you start: You need the Manage - System Settings access right. Go to Manage; Utilities; System Settings . At Look For , type part of the setting name or its Id to filter the Settings List . Select the setting to see its Name , Type and Description . To set it for the whole company, enter the Value under Company Settings Info . To set it for one store, enter the Value next to that store under Location Settings Info . A store value overrides the company value for that store. Select Save . Select Yes at \"Would you like to refresh your user session for these changes to take effect?\" Note: Other users, and anyone who selected No, need to select Help; Refresh User Session or log out and back in before the change takes effect for them. Note: Some settings are managed by TCS and don't appear in the list. Some appear only after the feature they belong to is turned on for your company. Examples of settings stores commonly use: Transfer Pricing Source , Reorder Point Calculation Method , Inventory Receipt - Populate Quantity Received and Engine Oil Non-Catalog Requires Sourcing ."}, {"u": "technicians-setup-and-maintenance.html", "t": "Technicians Setup and Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Technicians Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Use Technicians to set up the people who do the work. A technician can be a technician only, or can also have a user ID if they'll perform any duties in the application. Each skill level holds its own labor rate. See Labor Rate Setup and Maintenance . Go to Manage; Company Setup; Technicians ."}, {"u": "technicians-setup-and-maintenance.html#create-a-technician", "t": "Create a technician", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Technicians Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Select Add . A window displays \"Added a New Technician Record\". On the Technician Details tab, select a User Id only if the technician will also use the application. Otherwise, leave it blank. Enter the Initials (up to 4 characters). Enter the Last Name . Enter the First Name . Select the Skill Level . Enter the Clock ID Number , if applicable. Make sure the status is set to active. Select Save . \"Save Operation Successful\" displays."}, {"u": "technicians-setup-and-maintenance.html#assign-stores-to-a-technician", "t": "Assign stores to a technician", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Technicians Setup and Maintenance", "x": "On the Location tab, select the stores. To select several stores, hold CTRL and select each one. Select Add All if you want all stores. The stores display in the Associated Locations box below Available Locations . Make sure Active is checked next to each store you added. Select Save . \"Save Operation Successful\" displays."}, {"u": "technicians-setup-and-maintenance.html#change-a-technician", "t": "Change a technician", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Technicians Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Select the technician in the list first. The list is sorted alphabetically by initials. To inactivate a technician: On the Technician Details tab, clear the active status and select Save . \"Save Operation Successful\" displays. To change the skill level: Select the skill level and select Save . \"Save Operation Successful\" displays. To add stores, follow the steps in Assign stores to a technician above. To remove stores: In the Associated Locations box, select the stores to remove. To select several stores, hold CTRL and select each one. Select Remove , or Remove All to remove every store. Select Save . \"Save Operation Successful\" displays. Note: By default, the list shows only active technicians. To show all of them, check Show Inactive Technicians below the technician list."}, {"u": "unlocking-objects.html", "t": "Unlocking Objects", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Unlocking Objects", "x": "Use Unlock Objects to unlock orders, invoices, receipts and purchase orders when a warning says another user has them locked. Before you start: You can add this function to any access group. Select the access group, find the UNLOCK OBJECTS Group Name, and check the boxes for view, edit or both. Setting or changing access rights is generally a job for the Administrator access group. Go to Manage; Utilities; Unlock Objects . The Manage Object Locks window displays. Locks are listed by store number and then by document type. Check the lines to unlock. You can select several. Select . A message confirms that the lines unlocked successfully."}, {"u": "vendors-setup-and-maintenance.html", "t": "Vendors Setup and Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › Vendors Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Set up vendors in Manage; Company Setup; Vendors . To map brands for replenishment, see Vendor Replenishment . To order electronically, see Vendor Ordering . Vendor Type : Picks the electronic ordering integration the vendor uses, such as Michelin BWS, ATD, TCS Partner or Bridgestone Treadnet. This is set with TCS when the integration is turned on. Active : Clear it to deactivate a vendor. Check it again to reactivate. Requires EDIT on the Vendors - Deactivate/Reactivate access right. Show Inactive Vendors : Check it to include inactive vendors in the list. Select Save after you make changes."}, {"u": "user-setup-and-maintenance.html", "t": "User Setup and Maintenance", "p": "Section 6: Manage › User Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Use User Setup to create users and salespersons. Go to Manage; Company Setup; Users ."}, {"u": "user-setup-and-maintenance.html#create-a-user", "t": "Create a user", "p": "Section 6: Manage › User Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Select Add . On the Details tab, enter the User ID you want. This is generally the first initial and last name in all caps. Enter a Password . Enter the Name (first and last name). Enter an Email Address , if applicable. Select a default printer if you want. Turn Exact Id Search on or off. Turn Dialog Pop Up Active on or off. Make sure Active is on. It's on by default. Select Save . \"Successfully Saved\" displays. To copy settings from another user, select that user in Copy User settings from . Do this only after the Details tab information is complete. A warning says this overwrites all settings of the user being created. Select Yes or No to continue. On the Pricing tab, turn on Allow Hand Pricing if you want. This lets the user override pricing when access rights don't permit it. Turn on Enforce Minimum Profit% and enter a percentage if you want. This lets the user override pricing down to the minimum profit percentage you set. Select the price levels the user can view and select . To select several, hold CTRL, make your selections, and then select . To select all, hold SHIFT, select the first and last levels, and then select . Select Save . \"Successfully Saved\" displays. On the Locations tab, select the stores the user can view and select . To select several, hold CTRL, make your selections, and then select . To select all, hold SHIFT, select the first and last stores, and then select . If the store list is long, use to search by ID or location name. Select Save . \"Successfully Saved\" displays. On the User Settings tab, select a skin from the dropdown. The default is black simple. Select the search font size. The default is medium. Turn on Hide Tire Search Results with Zero Quantity if you want. You can also turn this on or off on the search screen. Select the Service Package View Mode . The default is list view. Tabbed view is generally preferred. Turn on Hide Tire Search Results with Zero Warehouse Quantity if you want. You can also turn this on or off on the search screen. Turn on Hide Tire Search Results with Zero Distribution Quantity if you want. You can also turn this on or off on the search screen. Select Print Setup . The associated stores fill in from your selections on the Locations tab. You can set up printing differently for each associated store. Select the reports the user can print and select . To select several, hold CTRL, make your selections, and then select . To select all, hold SHIFT, select the first and last reports, and then select . Select a print option from the dropdown. Show Print Preview Skip Preview and Dialog : No print screen appears for viewing the document. Show Print Dialog Only Select the default printer name. Enter the number of copies to print for the report type. Turn on auto close if you want. This isn't recommended."}, {"u": "user-setup-and-maintenance.html#change-a-user", "t": "Change a user", "p": "Section 6: Manage › User Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Select the user in the list first. The list is sorted alphabetically by first name. Note: To include inactive users in the user list, turn on . Inactive users appear at the bottom of the list. To inactivate a user: On the Details tab, clear the active status and select Save . \"Successfully Saved\" displays. To reset a password: On the Details tab, select at Password . Enter the New Password . Enter the new password again. Select Change Password . To add price levels, stores or print options, follow the steps in Create a user above. To remove price levels, stores or print options: Select the entries you want to remove. To select several, hold CTRL and select each one. Select Remove , or Remove All to remove every entry. Select Save . \"Successfully Saved\" displays."}, {"u": "user-setup-and-maintenance.html#catalog-updates", "t": "Catalog updates", "p": "Section 6: Manage › User Setup and Maintenance", "x": "Parts and labor catalog data comes from the catalog your store is set up to use. Epicor ISE : Catalog data comes from Epicor's online service. Connection settings are under Manage; Company Setup; Epicor ISE Configuration and are normally set by TCS. TireGuide : Catalog data is maintained centrally by TCS. Catalog updates are handled with TCS Support. Contact TCS Support if catalog data looks out of date."}, {"u": "appendix-order-status-numbers.html", "t": "Appendix: Order Status Numbers", "p": "Appendix: Order Status Numbers › Appendix: Order Status Numbers", "x": "Support and integration partners refer to order statuses by number. A store can rename a status on the OrderState Labels tab, but its number stays the same. 5 : Quick Quote 7 : Appointment 10 : Open 20 : Estimate 30 : Approved 40 : Waiting For Parts 50 : Ready For Work 70 : Revised 80 : Work Complete 90 : Closed 91 : Memo 95 : Declined 98 : Canceled"}];